1
00:01:58,320 --> 00:02:08,850
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:09,199 --> 00:02:13,490
Episode 88

3
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,260
You vile dog!

4
00:03:32,430 --> 00:03:40,170
Umur, Ivaz, you, your tribe, the troop
you want to establish...

5
00:03:40,250 --> 00:03:43,900
...a rooted state, a mighty plane tree...

6
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:48,490
...I've heard all of these, Osman.

7
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:52,390
But you can't grow without light.

8
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:56,340
You will surrender to my darkness!

9
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:02,070
Who is under this mask?

10
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:09,720
We will see now.

11
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:14,279
Who are you?

12
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:34,440
You lived too long, Osman!

13
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:37,380
Too long!

14
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:40,420
But the time has come.

15
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:44,340
My Bey!

16
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:02,580
Master!

17
00:05:10,030 --> 00:05:11,400
Come on, brother!

18
00:05:53,110 --> 00:05:54,160
Barkın!

19
00:05:54,450 --> 00:05:56,860
Don't let go of the demon!
Come on!

20
00:06:01,450 --> 00:06:03,690
Who did this!
Who did this!

21
00:06:03,810 --> 00:06:04,660
Who!

22
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:06,030
In the name of Allah!

23
00:06:11,550 --> 00:06:12,940
Allah is the healer!

24
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:14,740
Allah is the healer!

25
00:06:15,340 --> 00:06:16,490
Allah is the healer!

26
00:06:18,390 --> 00:06:19,670
Akça!

27
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:21,310
Akça, bring the bowl!

28
00:06:21,500 --> 00:06:23,240
Bring the bowl!

29
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:32,200
Allah is the healer!

30
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:36,820
Hang on, my Sheik, hang on!

31
00:06:38,390 --> 00:06:39,250
The soup!

32
00:06:40,140 --> 00:06:41,120
Akça Dervish!

33
00:06:41,370 --> 00:06:42,920
Bring the soup!

34
00:06:49,870 --> 00:06:51,700
Hang on, my Sheik, hang on!

35
00:06:54,180 --> 00:06:57,800
Do you think it is the soup, Kumral Abdal?

36
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:05,260
Hang on, my Sheik, hang on!

37
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:13,580
The soup is poisoned!

38
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,710
What are you saying, Kumral Abdal?

39
00:07:16,350 --> 00:07:17,320
My Sheik!

40
00:07:19,410 --> 00:07:21,790
First Mari, Now my father.

41
00:07:25,630 --> 00:07:26,940
Kumral Abdal...

42
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:29,600
...Cornelia?

43
00:08:19,220 --> 00:08:22,030
We're in front of you, we're behind you.

44
00:08:22,390 --> 00:08:25,300
You will die, Osman!
You will die!

45
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:03,030
Come to me, infidels!

46
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,380
Well done, Cerkutay!

47
00:09:24,420 --> 00:09:25,200
Praise be!

48
00:09:25,350 --> 00:09:27,650
-To you too, brother.
-Come on.

49
00:09:27,730 --> 00:09:28,880
Come on.

50
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,260
Turan...

51
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:33,900
...go to the tribe.

52
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,610
Bring me Cornelia and Zehra.

53
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:36,910
Is something wrong?

54
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:37,710
Is Sheik fine?

55
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:38,670
Hurry, Turan!

56
00:09:38,750 --> 00:09:40,150
I want them!

57
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:21,820
Osman!

58
00:10:22,650 --> 00:10:24,510
If anything happens to my master...

59
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,720
...I will destroy Kayı upon your head!

60
00:10:44,920 --> 00:10:46,530
You vile dog!

61
00:10:47,910 --> 00:10:49,340
You vile dog!

62
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:50,990
You killed Ivaz Bey!

63
00:10:51,120 --> 00:10:52,610
You killed him!

64
00:10:52,710 --> 00:10:54,190
What are you doing?

65
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:56,610
What are you doing?

66
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:31,780
Malhun Hatun doesn't seem well.
She is ill, I guess.

67
00:11:31,900 --> 00:11:34,960
She will be better when she gets some
rest, I hope.

68
00:11:40,130 --> 00:11:42,080
Zehra Hatun, Sister Cornelia...

69
00:11:42,750 --> 00:11:44,820
...Bala Hatun wants to see you
immediately.

70
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:50,050
What is it?

71
00:11:50,250 --> 00:11:51,610
She said to come quickly.

72
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:53,340
That's all I know, Aygül Hatun.

73
00:12:21,510 --> 00:12:22,300
My Bey!

74
00:12:26,530 --> 00:12:27,520
You!

75
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:29,830
You made me lose that infidel!

76
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:30,940
You!

77
00:12:40,790 --> 00:12:42,360
I succumbed to my anger, my Bey.

78
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:46,450
He who can't control his anger
can't control anything!

79
00:12:52,500 --> 00:12:54,700
You let that traitor breathe!

80
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:55,930
You...

81
00:13:08,410 --> 00:13:09,480
Now...

82
00:13:10,530 --> 00:13:13,840
...take the martyrs and Ivaz Bey
to the tribe.

83
00:13:15,430 --> 00:13:17,480
Bury the martyrs at once!

84
00:13:18,570 --> 00:13:19,460
Come on!

85
00:13:20,950 --> 00:13:22,090
Yes, my Bey.

86
00:13:22,880 --> 00:13:24,890
I will enter the tribe with martyrs,
again.

87
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:27,300
This same is enough for me.

88
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:36,410
My Bey.

89
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,740
It has Harmankaya Seal.

90
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:41,280
This is Kosses's arrow.

91
00:14:01,690 --> 00:14:08,030
The union we formed obviously
broke the devil's game.

92
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:14,590
They attack from everywhere.

93
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:21,510
They attack from everywhere.

94
00:14:24,130 --> 00:14:26,960
Söğüt

95
00:14:31,370 --> 00:14:36,880
Death cup, wolfsbane...

96
00:14:37,380 --> 00:14:39,840
...it looks like they mixed various
poisons.

97
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:52,780
My Sheik!

98
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:54,310
My Sheik!

99
00:14:57,800 --> 00:15:00,020
Bala, is my Sheik all right?

100
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,580
Cornelia.

101
00:15:10,290 --> 00:15:12,990
The meal you brought poisoned my Sheik.

102
00:15:18,420 --> 00:15:19,660
Hatuns!

103
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,300
How did this happen?

104
00:15:21,790 --> 00:15:23,750
How did this happen, right, Cornelia?

105
00:15:24,070 --> 00:15:25,640
Those you touch get poisoned.

106
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:27,470
First, Mari...

107
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,030
...now, my father.

108
00:15:30,030 --> 00:15:32,540
I, I didn't do it.

109
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:35,460
How could I do such a thing?

110
00:15:35,610 --> 00:15:37,280
How could you think this?

111
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:39,550
Would you say even if you did?

112
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:42,790
Those you breathe near get poisoned!

113
00:15:43,340 --> 00:15:44,430
Who?

114
00:15:45,060 --> 00:15:46,940
Who did this?

115
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,320
Who do you work for?

116
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:56,190
I didn't do it.

117
00:15:56,530 --> 00:15:59,740
I didn't even touch the meal, Bala Hatun!

118
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:04,400
Then, was it you, Zehra?

119
00:16:04,820 --> 00:16:07,230
Who else touched the soup?

120
00:16:08,140 --> 00:16:10,100
I didn't do it.

121
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,670
I made the soup with Selcen Mother.

122
00:16:13,330 --> 00:16:16,020
But I swear I didn't do such a thing.

123
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:20,660
You didn't, she didn't!

124
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:21,900
Who did?

125
00:16:22,650 --> 00:16:24,860
Who did this to my father?

126
00:16:24,910 --> 00:16:26,810
Who did?

127
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:28,610
Bala Hatun!

128
00:16:29,490 --> 00:16:30,740
Bala Hatun!

129
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:36,720
We don't say it is you, sisters.

130
00:16:38,820 --> 00:16:41,330
But the enemy is everywhere.

131
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:43,610
Zehra Hatun?

132
00:16:45,870 --> 00:16:47,060
Cornelia?

133
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:51,990
Didn't you leave the soup ever?

134
00:16:52,230 --> 00:16:53,130
No.

135
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:57,700
Zehra carried it all the way.

136
00:16:59,170 --> 00:17:01,480
She didn't let anyone touch it.

137
00:17:02,859 --> 00:17:03,869
Zehra...

138
00:17:04,420 --> 00:17:06,940
...if you didn't then who did?

139
00:17:07,910 --> 00:17:08,790
Get out!

140
00:17:09,329 --> 00:17:10,900
Get out and think!

141
00:17:10,990 --> 00:17:12,920
Think about who did this!

142
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:15,310
Get out!

143
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:26,480
Bala...

144
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:29,910
...you suspect Cornelia as well, right?

145
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:32,930
Is there anyone else to suspect, Aygül?

146
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:33,900
What about Mari?

147
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:36,760
Did she kill Mari too?

148
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:38,710
How?

149
00:17:41,070 --> 00:17:42,970
Keep an eye on her, Aygül.

150
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:45,770
Follow where she goes, whom she sees.

151
00:17:46,110 --> 00:17:47,860
We need to find who it is.

152
00:17:48,010 --> 00:17:49,260
We will.

153
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,510
We will, Bala.

154
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:55,190
The evil clearly has entered the tribe,
Bala Hatun.

155
00:17:56,230 --> 00:17:58,130
We must inform Osman Bey.

156
00:17:58,230 --> 00:17:59,780
Don't worry.

157
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,360
We will find out who it is.

158
00:18:10,990 --> 00:18:13,520
İnegöl Castle

159
00:18:29,850 --> 00:18:32,040
Osman is up to something.

160
00:18:33,810 --> 00:18:36,540
Where is Gündüz's grave, Nikola?

161
00:18:37,760 --> 00:18:39,310
Did Kosses burn him?

162
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:41,380
Did you hear such a thing?

163
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:44,620
Kosses loves to show off.

164
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:49,350
He should have killed Gündüz and throw his
head in front of Osman already.

165
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:51,910
They just said he died.

166
00:18:52,680 --> 00:18:53,840
All right.

167
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:56,730
Maybe Kosses took his revenge quietly.

168
00:18:58,020 --> 00:18:59,810
Maybe Gündüz is alive.

169
00:19:00,590 --> 00:19:02,060
And all of this is a game.

170
00:19:02,830 --> 00:19:05,790
Osman, Master Arius.

171
00:19:06,630 --> 00:19:10,450
Nothing about him surprises me.

172
00:19:10,890 --> 00:19:18,240
But an enemy he can't see will drive him
to highly doubtç

173
00:19:22,710 --> 00:19:25,620
I, Aya Nikola...

174
00:19:28,790 --> 00:19:32,640
...swear on the Ceasar's name that...

175
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:47,380
...Osman will already be ruined before he
finds out who you are.

176
00:19:51,180 --> 00:19:58,620
The darkness pays dearly for the service
rendered to it, Nkola.

177
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:05,240
Now the first thing we will do is
to clear Osman's doubts.

178
00:20:05,550 --> 00:20:07,760
What do you have in mind, Master?

179
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:10,800
I will resurrect what I killed, Nikola.

180
00:20:12,940 --> 00:20:16,340
I will give breath to Sheik Edebalı...

181
00:20:17,570 --> 00:20:19,750
...whom I left breathless.

182
00:20:33,130 --> 00:20:35,630
The owner of this arrow isn't Kosses.

183
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:38,990
Alps.

184
00:20:39,880 --> 00:20:41,580
Mari Hatun's death...

185
00:20:42,330 --> 00:20:44,240
...the slander thrown at Gündüz Bey...

186
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:49,750
...it is all to get Kosses and Turgut Bey
against us...

187
00:20:49,930 --> 00:20:52,260
...and to eliminate my brother.

188
00:20:57,640 --> 00:21:01,980
Their intention is to leave Kayı alone
and...

189
00:21:02,330 --> 00:21:04,150
...stop the conquests!

190
00:21:07,390 --> 00:21:09,270
Whoever did this...

191
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:13,420
...is the one who killed Ivaz Bey and
Umur Bey!

192
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:17,840
My Bey...

193
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,470
...did Gündüz Bey...

194
00:21:21,610 --> 00:21:23,440
...die because of slander?

195
00:21:26,590 --> 00:21:28,090
Gündüz Bey is alive.

196
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,080
He is now at the Kosses's castle.

197
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,600
Don't worry.

198
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:44,920
Thankfully!

199
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:48,640
So...

200
00:21:49,210 --> 00:21:50,160
...my Bey...

201
00:21:50,410 --> 00:21:52,100
...then who is doing all these?

202
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:53,330
Who is the traitor?

203
00:21:53,420 --> 00:21:55,220
We will find out, Boran.

204
00:21:56,360 --> 00:21:58,940
If you don't know where the trouble
comes from...

205
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:01,950
...you'll take a look at when it comes.

206
00:22:07,770 --> 00:22:08,980
Barkın...

207
00:22:10,680 --> 00:22:13,050
...and İbrahim Faki.

208
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:18,040
So, those two demons did all these?

209
00:22:21,830 --> 00:22:23,860
Trouble began with their arrival.

210
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:26,320
We will act with doubt.

211
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:27,800
Başsungur.

212
00:22:28,030 --> 00:22:28,790
My Bey?

213
00:22:29,050 --> 00:22:30,700
You will be after Barkın.

214
00:22:33,190 --> 00:22:34,030
Saltuk.

215
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:34,740
My Bey?

216
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:37,510
You will always watch İbrahim Faki.

217
00:22:38,670 --> 00:22:40,890
Since they come from the darkness...

218
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:44,300
...you will be shadows.

219
00:22:45,310 --> 00:22:46,360
Yes, my Bey.

220
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:47,800
Yes, my Bey.

221
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:48,850
Alps...

222
00:22:49,310 --> 00:22:51,690
...you will be on alert.

223
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,630
They plant the seeds of discord...

224
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:56,240
...and spill our brothers' blood.

225
00:22:59,120 --> 00:23:01,640
If it all comes down to you...

226
00:23:02,050 --> 00:23:06,340
...then you won't believe what
you see and hear.

227
00:23:06,590 --> 00:23:07,730
No one...

228
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:09,680
...will act without asking me.

229
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:11,220
Yes, my Bey!

230
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:14,610
We are going to Harmankaya.

231
00:23:14,850 --> 00:23:15,620
Come on!

232
00:23:50,120 --> 00:23:52,490
Both Turgut and Kosses.

233
00:23:52,790 --> 00:23:55,980
We will cut off both of Osman's arms!

234
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:57,850
He will be alone.

235
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:01,670
But lone wolves are dangerous as well,
Nikola.

236
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:05,280
I'll pull out his teeth too.

237
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:08,000
He won't even be able to growl.

238
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:12,130
But first, he has to attack Kosses
with anger.

239
00:24:15,280 --> 00:24:17,630
Kosses won't want to be harmed
and...

240
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:19,040
...will come to us.

241
00:24:19,490 --> 00:24:24,150
Besides, Argus and my soldiers already
settled in Harmankaya.

242
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:29,580
We will not only turn Kosses and
Turgut against Osman but also...

243
00:24:29,650 --> 00:24:32,100
...we will take them on our side.

244
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:33,810
Not yet.

245
00:24:34,460 --> 00:24:38,580
First, I will wait for Osman to make
a move against Kosses.

246
00:24:38,810 --> 00:24:41,280
I will wait for news from my spy.

247
00:24:45,110 --> 00:24:46,440
Soldier.

248
00:25:01,600 --> 00:25:03,030
Excuse me.

249
00:25:13,530 --> 00:25:14,620
Precaution.

250
00:25:22,090 --> 00:25:24,800
The gold you wanted, Master Arius.

251
00:25:25,210 --> 00:25:28,550
But you didn't tell me what you wanted
it for.

252
00:25:29,380 --> 00:25:33,180
To drown the Turks in the palm of
darkness, Nikola.

253
00:25:34,290 --> 00:25:36,520
This gold will go to Barkın.

254
00:25:36,900 --> 00:25:40,280
Barkın, who will be the bey of
Kızılbey Oğulları.

255
00:25:41,010 --> 00:25:44,350
Barkın is with Osman but he is one of us.

256
00:25:44,980 --> 00:25:47,600
Most brutal warrior of the darkness.

257
00:25:48,170 --> 00:25:51,040
A knight to tear the Turks to pieces.

258
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:57,280
This gold will be one of his most powerful
weapons for this cause.

259
00:25:58,990 --> 00:26:02,200
Harmankaya Castle.

260
00:26:38,750 --> 00:26:41,640
You! Where are you going?
Stop!

261
00:26:50,010 --> 00:26:51,400
Go on.

262
00:27:00,440 --> 00:27:01,700
Come on, Osman Bey.

263
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:05,690
Thank you, Samuel.

264
00:27:06,030 --> 00:27:07,040
I will go now.

265
00:27:07,220 --> 00:27:08,240
Here you go.

266
00:27:40,270 --> 00:27:41,490
Here he is.

267
00:28:16,010 --> 00:28:17,630
Ivaz Bey is dead...

268
00:28:23,180 --> 00:28:24,410
...Kosses.

269
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:33,170
This arrow is ours.

270
00:28:33,810 --> 00:28:35,060
Where did you find it?

271
00:28:35,130 --> 00:28:37,820
It fell in front of me as I took off
the mask...

272
00:28:38,510 --> 00:28:39,960
... from the devil's face.

273
00:28:43,180 --> 00:28:45,590
They want to get their job done.

274
00:28:46,030 --> 00:28:47,810
First, they turned you against us...

275
00:28:48,110 --> 00:28:50,180
...now they want to turn Kosses
against you.

276
00:28:51,020 --> 00:28:52,900
You are right, Turgut Bey.

277
00:28:53,420 --> 00:28:54,940
Who attacked you?

278
00:28:55,030 --> 00:28:56,400
Isn't there any other trace?

279
00:28:56,490 --> 00:28:58,310
Whoever killed Mari attacked.

280
00:28:59,840 --> 00:29:01,850
Whoever burned the Söğüt attacked.

281
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:05,360
Whoever killed Ivaz Bey...

282
00:29:05,820 --> 00:29:07,580
...attacked.

283
00:29:08,740 --> 00:29:12,770
But now I am after those I suspect.

284
00:29:14,390 --> 00:29:15,630
Where is my brother?

285
00:29:16,240 --> 00:29:17,460
Samuel.

286
00:29:43,210 --> 00:29:44,570
Kosses.

287
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:49,240
It's only natural for me to tie the hands
of someone I think...

288
00:29:49,540 --> 00:29:52,050
...is responsible for my brother's death,
Osman Bey.

289
00:30:01,310 --> 00:30:02,080
Brother.

290
00:30:02,120 --> 00:30:03,555
Brother.

291
00:30:07,220 --> 00:30:09,550
You will continue to seem dead.

292
00:30:11,220 --> 00:30:13,720
You won't come to the tribe for a while.

293
00:30:14,050 --> 00:30:16,570
We agree until the truth comes out,
my Bey.

294
00:30:16,920 --> 00:30:18,820
What will we do now, Osman Bey?

295
00:30:19,350 --> 00:30:21,620
Now, it is your turn, Turgut Bey.

296
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:28,550
Kosses proved he is against me by killing
my brother and attacking me.

297
00:30:31,320 --> 00:30:33,350
You will be against me too.

298
00:30:34,250 --> 00:30:37,350
They'll think we're at each other's
throats with our swords.

299
00:30:38,170 --> 00:30:40,470
We do whatever it takes.

300
00:30:40,650 --> 00:30:42,470
What it takes is the conquest.

301
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:47,920
They set all the traps to stop
the conquest.

302
00:30:49,500 --> 00:30:52,620
We won't stop so that we be victorious.

303
00:30:52,950 --> 00:30:55,220
Of course, don't worry.

304
00:30:56,250 --> 00:30:58,750
So, how do we do this?

305
00:31:00,450 --> 00:31:03,020
Thanks to you and Turgut Bey.

306
00:31:05,570 --> 00:31:09,100
The Lord of Inhisar is Nikola's ally.

307
00:31:10,220 --> 00:31:14,700
Only support force coming from the east
will be from there.

308
00:31:16,700 --> 00:31:19,920
Inhisar is important.
We will take it first.

309
00:31:20,170 --> 00:31:22,620
Without any battle preparations.

310
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:26,800
Later we will arrive at Inegöl's doors.

311
00:31:37,620 --> 00:31:39,720
Couldn't you find it yet, Kumral Abdal?

312
00:31:40,270 --> 00:31:42,570
The antidote I gave doesn't help.

313
00:31:43,950 --> 00:31:46,070
My Sheik will die in my hands.

314
00:31:48,820 --> 00:31:50,500
My Allah, protect him!

315
00:31:51,170 --> 00:31:53,920
My Allah, who gave the cure to
Prophet Eyüp...

316
00:31:54,750 --> 00:31:56,450
...help us.

317
00:31:56,970 --> 00:31:59,050
Don't leave us in the dark.

318
00:32:00,420 --> 00:32:03,850
-Show us the way.
-Amen.

319
00:32:09,350 --> 00:32:11,050
May peace be with you.

320
00:32:12,150 --> 00:32:15,020
-May peace be with you.
-May peace be with you.

321
00:32:18,150 --> 00:32:22,920
Bala Hatun, Akça Dervish told me.
How is he?

322
00:32:26,350 --> 00:32:29,200
Who would want to hurt, Sheik Edebalı?

323
00:32:31,450 --> 00:32:33,400
We don't know, İbrahim Faki.

324
00:32:37,020 --> 00:32:40,070
Let my Sheik get rid of the claws of
this poison...

325
00:32:42,970 --> 00:32:45,020
... then the time will come
for reckoning.

326
00:32:51,670 --> 00:32:55,550
It's like they mixed all kinds of poisons
and put them in, İbrahim Faki.

327
00:32:55,700 --> 00:32:57,650
The antidote doesn't work.

328
00:32:58,320 --> 00:33:00,100
I don't know what to do.

329
00:33:03,550 --> 00:33:05,300
I am here, Kumral Abdal!

330
00:33:09,300 --> 00:33:10,920
I found what you asked for.

331
00:33:13,370 --> 00:33:14,870
What is that?

332
00:33:16,500 --> 00:33:17,670
Ground hele.

333
00:33:19,100 --> 00:33:20,900
It may work.

334
00:33:22,300 --> 00:33:24,400
I hope the healing from them.

335
00:33:26,950 --> 00:33:29,420
Do you know what he was poisoned with?

336
00:33:30,800 --> 00:33:32,870
We don't know who did it and how but...

337
00:33:34,220 --> 00:33:35,900
...the food was poisoned.

338
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:01,350
It is as you said, Kumral Abdal.

339
00:34:02,520 --> 00:34:04,320
This is really strong.

340
00:34:06,320 --> 00:34:09,199
I know a poison like this but...

341
00:34:10,620 --> 00:34:12,969
...there is no one here who may know it.

342
00:34:16,520 --> 00:34:18,820
I've seen it used a lot in the east.

343
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:21,719
It killed those it poisoned in one night.

344
00:34:21,719 --> 00:34:23,719
Heaven forbid, İbrahim Faki!

345
00:34:24,370 --> 00:34:25,949
Isn't there a cure?

346
00:34:27,250 --> 00:34:29,320
We will find one, I hope.

347
00:34:34,170 --> 00:34:37,800
Kumral Abdal, you did your best.

348
00:34:38,449 --> 00:34:40,500
Let me try this time.

349
00:35:43,060 --> 00:35:44,900
You neither could protect my father...

350
00:35:45,670 --> 00:35:46,800
...nor my uncle.

351
00:35:48,100 --> 00:35:50,200
Is this how you keep your promise, Barkın?

352
00:35:50,570 --> 00:35:51,600
Don't, my Selvi.

353
00:35:52,600 --> 00:35:53,600
Don't.

354
00:35:54,500 --> 00:35:56,100
Don't hurt me even more.

355
00:35:59,850 --> 00:36:01,620
My heart burns, Barkın.

356
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:04,870
I have no one left.

357
00:36:06,520 --> 00:36:10,450
My father is gone, Barkın!

358
00:36:12,170 --> 00:36:13,600
You have me, Selvi.

359
00:36:14,200 --> 00:36:16,120
Am I not your family?

360
00:36:16,770 --> 00:36:18,300
What did I do wrong?

361
00:36:21,650 --> 00:36:26,120
Why did Ivaz Bey and Uğur Bey set off?

362
00:36:27,100 --> 00:36:28,750
Because of Osman.

363
00:36:29,470 --> 00:36:30,690
He couldn't protect them.

364
00:36:31,550 --> 00:36:34,370
Osman is one who could not clean
his lands from the enemies.

365
00:36:35,470 --> 00:36:38,400
Are we guilty for it?

366
00:36:41,320 --> 00:36:42,850
My Selvi...

367
00:36:44,220 --> 00:36:46,820
...Osman could not recognize
his traitor brother.

368
00:36:47,850 --> 00:36:49,850
Why am I guilty for it?

369
00:36:54,250 --> 00:36:56,370
Why did we come here, Barkın?

370
00:36:57,020 --> 00:36:59,120
For all this pain?

371
00:37:00,720 --> 00:37:02,000
My Selvi...

372
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:05,900
...there is no turning back now.

373
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:12,000
When the day comes, I will take revenge
on Osman...

374
00:37:14,070 --> 00:37:15,800
...who caused your father's death...

375
00:37:16,500 --> 00:37:21,070
...and on those who killed your father.

376
00:37:24,470 --> 00:37:26,120
Promise me, Barkın.

377
00:37:26,450 --> 00:37:29,970
You will avenge both my father and
my uncle!

378
00:37:30,700 --> 00:37:32,370
I promise, Selvi.

379
00:37:33,500 --> 00:37:36,300
I won't die before I take their revenge.

380
00:37:37,370 --> 00:37:38,870
But...

381
00:37:39,770 --> 00:37:44,200
...I won't leave Ivaz Bey's tribe
without a leader.

382
00:37:45,870 --> 00:37:48,220
Your father's will was for me to the Bey.

383
00:37:48,920 --> 00:37:50,220
I will be.

384
00:37:51,270 --> 00:37:56,420
Even the Kızılbey Oğulları will see
the truth at the assembly.

385
00:37:59,770 --> 00:38:02,470
Come here, my Selvi.

386
00:38:07,550 --> 00:38:11,850
I want to marry you after the assembly.

387
00:38:13,700 --> 00:38:15,370
What are you saying, Barkın?

388
00:38:15,970 --> 00:38:20,150
I just buried my father! What marriage
are you talking about?

389
00:38:20,470 --> 00:38:22,640
Your father would want this as well,
my Selvi.

390
00:38:24,570 --> 00:38:29,250
The Beys won't take me seriously until
our wedding is done.

391
00:38:30,370 --> 00:38:32,300
Now we will get married.

392
00:38:32,300 --> 00:38:36,720
It is my duty to Ivaz Bey to make
a wedding worthy of us...

393
00:38:37,100 --> 00:38:39,120
...after our mourning is over.

394
00:39:03,300 --> 00:39:06,070
He is opening his eyes! Thankfully!

395
00:39:06,170 --> 00:39:09,350
Father! Father!

396
00:39:09,600 --> 00:39:11,100
Praise be!

397
00:39:11,750 --> 00:39:13,770
Praise be!

398
00:39:15,170 --> 00:39:17,520
Thank you, my Allah!

399
00:39:17,870 --> 00:39:19,520
My Sheik?

400
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:23,270
Get better soon, my Sheik.

401
00:39:26,370 --> 00:39:28,420
Thank you, İbrahim Faki.

402
00:39:33,570 --> 00:39:36,550
You are a savior!
A savior!

403
00:39:37,570 --> 00:39:39,870
How can I ever repay you...

404
00:39:40,420 --> 00:39:43,670
...now that you healed my Sheik?

405
00:39:47,650 --> 00:39:50,250
Our home is now your home, İbrahim Faki.

406
00:39:50,420 --> 00:39:52,720
We owe you a life.

407
00:39:52,720 --> 00:39:55,570
Don't mention it. It is nothing.

408
00:39:57,000 --> 00:40:00,750
I will go to the tavern now. I will visit
you later, I hope.

409
00:40:11,800 --> 00:40:15,150
Zehra. Cornelia.
Head to the tribe.

410
00:40:15,150 --> 00:40:17,700
You go.
I'll stay with Bala Hatun.

411
00:40:46,250 --> 00:40:49,070
My bey, I'm watching Barkın.

412
00:40:49,300 --> 00:40:51,300
He received two chests of
gold today.

413
00:40:52,120 --> 00:40:53,550
From whom?

414
00:40:54,250 --> 00:40:57,820
I don't know, my bey.
Someone must've left it earlier.

415
00:40:59,620 --> 00:41:04,020
Whoever pays him the coins
receives his service.

416
00:41:04,800 --> 00:41:08,020
-Keep your eyes on him.
-As you order.

417
00:41:28,770 --> 00:41:31,020
He who creates
by just saying...

418
00:41:32,420 --> 00:41:36,600
who fills our heart with
the goodness of faith...

419
00:41:37,600 --> 00:41:40,800
great Allah's ninety-nine names!

420
00:41:44,250 --> 00:41:48,850
With the name of Allah!

421
00:41:50,250 --> 00:41:54,050
Umur Bey and İhvaz Bey.

422
00:41:56,770 --> 00:42:01,320
They were riding to these borders
to help us.

423
00:42:02,500 --> 00:42:04,470
They killed them.

424
00:42:05,570 --> 00:42:07,050
Barkın Bey...

425
00:42:08,500 --> 00:42:11,520
said that Mongols killed Umur Bey.

426
00:42:15,970 --> 00:42:18,120
And when we reached İhvaz Bey...

427
00:42:19,350 --> 00:42:21,960
we found Kosses' arrows.

428
00:42:27,050 --> 00:42:31,720
My bey. We took Kosses to our tribe.
We should've expected it from the heathen.

429
00:42:32,070 --> 00:42:37,120
Kosses, Nikola; we worked with one heathen
to beat the other.

430
00:42:37,670 --> 00:42:41,850
The attack at Söğüt. Do we know
who did it?

431
00:42:42,250 --> 00:42:44,200
Don't worry.

432
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:46,550
We will find it.

433
00:42:47,320 --> 00:42:51,720
Those who attack us without
honor will surely pay.

434
00:42:51,720 --> 00:42:54,050
You will, Osman Bey?

435
00:42:57,620 --> 00:43:01,450
You couldn't make the murderer of my
wife and baby pay.

436
00:43:03,490 --> 00:43:06,420
If Kosses, who you see as an enemy
now didn't kill him...

437
00:43:06,800 --> 00:43:09,210
justice wouldn't be served.

438
00:43:09,510 --> 00:43:10,830
Turgut.

439
00:43:12,130 --> 00:43:14,130
You are in the bey's tent.

440
00:43:15,430 --> 00:43:20,250
Know your words and position.

441
00:43:27,520 --> 00:43:29,710
You couldn't protect, Osman Bey.

442
00:43:31,260 --> 00:43:34,040
Is it a lie?
You couldn't protect.

443
00:43:34,420 --> 00:43:38,100
The beys who follow you get
hunted down one by one.

444
00:43:39,750 --> 00:43:41,080
Umur Bey.

445
00:43:41,350 --> 00:43:42,810
İhvaz Bey.

446
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:44,730
They were all warriors.

447
00:43:44,950 --> 00:43:47,160
You couldn't protect Söğüt either.

448
00:43:49,760 --> 00:43:53,820
Even Sheik Edebali is
facing death.

449
00:43:55,900 --> 00:44:01,560
Now, after losing the lives,
your settling scores don't matter.

450
00:44:02,750 --> 00:44:06,830
Are you afraid that the people
who are close to me are hunted?

451
00:44:08,260 --> 00:44:12,670
One who is afraid to be a prey
can't become a hunter.

452
00:44:13,490 --> 00:44:16,060
I was silent because
you were in pain.

453
00:44:17,190 --> 00:44:18,570
But...

454
00:44:20,280 --> 00:44:23,030
get out of my face now!

455
00:44:29,070 --> 00:44:30,390
Get out!

456
00:44:33,400 --> 00:44:35,180
Alright.

457
00:44:40,100 --> 00:44:42,540
Am I allowed, Osman bey?

458
00:44:46,760 --> 00:44:48,140
İhvaz Bey...

459
00:44:48,790 --> 00:44:50,220
Umur Bey...

460
00:44:50,630 --> 00:44:52,850
we all share that pain.

461
00:44:53,250 --> 00:44:54,140
But...

462
00:44:54,440 --> 00:44:57,530
my heart is burning
the most for them.

463
00:44:58,120 --> 00:45:00,340
They are attacking from
all sides.

464
00:45:01,100 --> 00:45:03,750
Osman Bey is on the righteous
path.

465
00:45:04,830 --> 00:45:07,810
Beys, the point is...

466
00:45:08,290 --> 00:45:10,590
the three that bears fruit will
be stoned.

467
00:45:11,650 --> 00:45:13,300
Thank you.

468
00:45:17,900 --> 00:45:19,220
Alps.

469
00:45:20,840 --> 00:45:23,820
Turgut Bey will never come to this tribe.

470
00:45:24,820 --> 00:45:27,310
If he comes near...

471
00:45:27,530 --> 00:45:29,880
you will drive him away.

472
00:45:33,750 --> 00:45:37,100
He has no value in my eyes now.

473
00:45:37,640 --> 00:45:41,080
As you order, my bey.

474
00:45:43,730 --> 00:45:45,300
The council is over.

475
00:45:48,410 --> 00:45:49,490
Come on.

476
00:46:10,300 --> 00:46:14,680
I can't understand it, Cornelia?
How did this happen?

477
00:46:15,220 --> 00:46:16,840
I don't know, Zehra.

478
00:46:17,090 --> 00:46:18,840
I don't know.

479
00:46:25,470 --> 00:46:28,260
Let's stop by the marketplace.

480
00:46:28,560 --> 00:46:31,750
I'll wait by the horses. You take care
of your business and come.

481
00:46:31,970 --> 00:46:33,100
Alright.

482
00:46:48,950 --> 00:46:52,710
Forgive me. I'm checking if İbrahim
Fakıh is inside.

483
00:46:53,070 --> 00:46:55,450
He left before me.
Didn't you see?

484
00:46:55,660 --> 00:46:58,500
I went to the marketplace.
He must have left then.

485
00:46:58,720 --> 00:47:01,750
-Thank you.
-Thank you, too.

486
00:47:19,850 --> 00:47:22,820
I don't have much time.
Zehra is waiting.

487
00:47:23,170 --> 00:47:25,260
Why did you save him, sir?

488
00:47:25,720 --> 00:47:28,210
You said that we would kill him.

489
00:47:28,750 --> 00:47:31,800
You said that the light
of the Oghuz would fade.

490
00:47:31,940 --> 00:47:34,160
Pretty Cornelia.

491
00:47:34,320 --> 00:47:38,730
Kumral noticed the poison. It was a
matter of time to find the antidote.

492
00:47:39,000 --> 00:47:41,870
We couldn't make that fool a hero.

493
00:47:42,330 --> 00:47:45,900
If someone will profit from
this chaos...

494
00:47:46,090 --> 00:47:48,930
it should always be us.

495
00:47:49,770 --> 00:47:56,800
And saving Edebali is the best way
to gain their trust.

496
00:47:58,830 --> 00:48:00,180
Right.

497
00:48:00,590 --> 00:48:03,160
They'll trust you more now.

498
00:48:03,460 --> 00:48:06,320
Everything is for our holy cause.

499
00:48:06,620 --> 00:48:11,520
You will get close into
the hearts of them.

500
00:48:11,730 --> 00:48:14,900
Don't worry.
I'm working on it.

501
00:48:15,300 --> 00:48:16,330
But...

502
00:48:16,820 --> 00:48:18,010
But?

503
00:48:19,470 --> 00:48:21,200
Bala is suspicious of me.

504
00:48:21,360 --> 00:48:24,470
This last move took all the
attentions to me.

505
00:48:24,830 --> 00:48:27,400
Then, Beautiful Cornelia.

506
00:48:27,610 --> 00:48:30,290
It's time for our next move.

507
00:48:33,480 --> 00:48:35,000
But...

508
00:48:35,380 --> 00:48:38,270
this will be painful.

509
00:49:17,230 --> 00:49:20,340
Saltuk. What are you doing here?

510
00:49:21,660 --> 00:49:24,210
I'm following İbrahim Fakih
by my bey's orders.

511
00:49:24,500 --> 00:49:26,370
But I lost his track.

512
00:49:26,560 --> 00:49:28,240
Have you seen him, Aygül Hatun?

513
00:49:28,910 --> 00:49:31,160
He left the lodge.

514
00:49:32,510 --> 00:49:34,840
I hope it's good.

515
00:49:45,420 --> 00:49:48,420
Now, we have a clue
on our suspicions.

516
00:49:48,690 --> 00:49:49,880
Alps...

517
00:49:50,100 --> 00:49:52,800
are following the master and
Barkın.

518
00:49:53,100 --> 00:49:57,370
But during this time, we won't
be staying idle here.

519
00:49:58,970 --> 00:50:00,190
Konur.

520
00:50:01,110 --> 00:50:02,460
Speak.

521
00:50:02,780 --> 00:50:05,080
Speak so that everyone
will hear it.

522
00:50:06,490 --> 00:50:09,440
İnhisar's lord valued
his life, my bey.

523
00:50:10,280 --> 00:50:11,320
Firstly...

524
00:50:11,350 --> 00:50:14,840
I told him that we surrounded
the castle.

525
00:50:14,930 --> 00:50:17,070
Then, I gave him our conditions.

526
00:50:17,800 --> 00:50:19,450
From now...

527
00:50:19,660 --> 00:50:21,940
we'll feed our animals on
their grass.

528
00:50:22,400 --> 00:50:26,060
No soldier will question the
ones who carry Kayı flag.

529
00:50:26,180 --> 00:50:28,950
In return for keeping his castle...

530
00:50:29,100 --> 00:50:31,510
they'll pay with two chests of gold
as a tribute.

531
00:50:31,840 --> 00:50:33,810
Mashallah.

532
00:50:38,360 --> 00:50:40,440
But tell me this.

533
00:50:40,930 --> 00:50:43,740
Did he accept all this voluntarily?

534
00:50:44,420 --> 00:50:49,010
What if someone opposes to this
agreement?

535
00:50:49,880 --> 00:50:52,860
When they say that they'll protect
him from Osman...

536
00:50:53,130 --> 00:50:54,940
will he accept it?

537
00:50:56,050 --> 00:50:59,190
Whoever it is that will protect
him from Osman...

538
00:50:59,400 --> 00:51:01,050
he'll jump right into it.

539
00:51:03,760 --> 00:51:05,460
Good.

540
00:51:09,360 --> 00:51:13,500
Now, our fake hostility with
Turgut Bey should be heard.

541
00:51:13,690 --> 00:51:20,210
Then, our enemies will go to
Kosses and Turgut Bey.

542
00:51:21,720 --> 00:51:24,890
When they sit at the table
as allies...

543
00:51:25,910 --> 00:51:29,920
we'll take İnhisar on that table.

544
00:51:31,810 --> 00:51:33,460
Inshallah.

545
00:51:34,140 --> 00:51:36,220
Thank Allah, my bey.

546
00:51:37,190 --> 00:51:40,410
It's time for conquest, my bey.

547
00:51:40,580 --> 00:51:41,960
Indeed.

548
00:51:42,820 --> 00:51:46,830
Our fresh weapons are waiting
to spell heathen blood, my bey.

549
00:51:46,990 --> 00:51:48,910
Thank you, Master Davud.

550
00:51:50,990 --> 00:51:53,050
May I enter, my bey?

551
00:51:53,320 --> 00:51:54,640
Come in.

552
00:52:00,160 --> 00:52:09,330
My bey. Bala Hatun sent news.
Sheik Edebali is poisoned.

553
00:52:14,010 --> 00:52:20,830
As you wanted. Malhun won't
wake up until you become the bey.

554
00:52:21,320 --> 00:52:22,910
Cornelia.

555
00:52:23,260 --> 00:52:25,670
You are really venomous.

556
00:52:26,050 --> 00:52:31,730
-How did you do it?
-I added some herbs to her water.

557
00:52:38,310 --> 00:52:41,390
Oh, my pretty girl.
You don't have fever either.

558
00:52:41,710 --> 00:52:43,850
What happened to you?

559
00:52:45,070 --> 00:52:49,800
I don't know, mother.
I can't stand up.

560
00:52:50,320 --> 00:52:52,450
I can't even open my eyes.

561
00:52:52,830 --> 00:52:54,920
Did she eat what I brought?

562
00:52:55,270 --> 00:52:57,050
She did, mother Selcan.

563
00:52:57,920 --> 00:53:01,490
Rest. I'll come again, my girl.

564
00:53:01,650 --> 00:53:03,190
Alright, mother.

565
00:53:04,840 --> 00:53:06,930
Stay with her.

566
00:53:19,630 --> 00:53:21,400
Malhun Hatun.

567
00:53:23,020 --> 00:53:24,600
Alaca.

568
00:53:51,500 --> 00:53:52,810
Thank you, my girl.

569
00:53:53,010 --> 00:53:53,710
Mother.

570
00:53:54,810 --> 00:53:56,200
How is Malhun?

571
00:53:56,520 --> 00:53:58,830
She barely ate now.

572
00:53:59,100 --> 00:54:01,200
But she hardly opens her eyes.

573
00:54:02,840 --> 00:54:05,290
Inshallah, she'll get up tomorrow.

574
00:54:05,490 --> 00:54:06,820
Inshallah.

575
00:54:07,450 --> 00:54:09,000
Sit.

576
00:54:19,510 --> 00:54:21,800
It's good to be cautious, mother.

577
00:54:22,300 --> 00:54:24,500
The enemy is close to us.

578
00:54:24,810 --> 00:54:26,210
True, my girl.

579
00:54:26,590 --> 00:54:28,210
We'll find them.

580
00:54:28,820 --> 00:54:30,210
We'll find them.

581
00:54:41,240 --> 00:54:42,990
Thank you, my girl.

582
00:54:51,380 --> 00:54:52,840
Cornelia.

583
00:54:55,270 --> 00:54:57,790
Come and sit, my girl.
Zehra will do it.

584
00:55:07,760 --> 00:55:09,310
Take a seat.

585
00:55:10,230 --> 00:55:11,290
Sit.

586
00:55:11,400 --> 00:55:12,460
Thank you.

587
00:55:28,970 --> 00:55:31,760
With the name of Allah.

588
00:55:37,720 --> 00:55:39,200
Come on.

589
00:55:56,800 --> 00:56:00,150
Söğüt

590
00:56:01,140 --> 00:56:03,240
Behold, my sheik!

591
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:17,370
The fake life...

592
00:56:29,060 --> 00:56:31,360
With the name of Allah.

593
00:56:38,420 --> 00:56:40,460
Salam Alaikum.

594
00:56:40,680 --> 00:56:45,600
Alaikum Salam.

595
00:56:56,200 --> 00:56:57,320
My sheik.

596
00:56:59,370 --> 00:57:02,180
May Allah always keep you
with us.

597
00:57:03,350 --> 00:57:06,950
Thank Allah, we are destined
to talk to you again.

598
00:57:08,440 --> 00:57:12,900
We are thankful to what
Allah gives us.

599
00:57:15,140 --> 00:57:16,540
Come on.

600
00:57:16,890 --> 00:57:19,300
With the name of Allah.

601
00:57:28,850 --> 00:57:33,510
Thank Allah for giving you
back to us.

602
00:57:34,040 --> 00:57:35,850
Thank you, Kumral Abdal.

603
00:57:37,470 --> 00:57:43,870
Inshallah, we'll sacrifice our
desires to Allah's way.

604
00:57:45,010 --> 00:57:47,270
And we'll be one of the
saved ones.

605
00:57:48,140 --> 00:57:49,350
Inshallah.

606
00:57:49,670 --> 00:57:53,860
How can we sacrifice our desires
for Allah's way?

607
00:57:55,630 --> 00:57:58,160
By standing away from the enemy, Akça.

608
00:57:59,620 --> 00:58:02,650
Will the enemies come to an
end in these lands, my sheik?

609
00:58:03,510 --> 00:58:07,250
A valiant has many enemies.

610
00:58:07,860 --> 00:58:09,200
Strong ones.

611
00:58:10,750 --> 00:58:17,140
A Muslim's greatest enemy is the devil.

612
00:58:19,980 --> 00:58:25,960
So, how much do we know
our enemy?

613
00:58:27,120 --> 00:58:31,350
He knows us very well.

614
00:58:32,520 --> 00:58:36,800
If we are a scholar, he makes us
brag about our science.

615
00:58:38,150 --> 00:58:39,550
If we are beautiful...

616
00:58:40,260 --> 00:58:45,240
our beauty flounder to
show itself.

617
00:58:46,960 --> 00:58:50,540
If we are rich, he makes us stingy.

618
00:58:50,940 --> 00:58:54,370
If we aren't, he makes us cruel.

619
00:58:55,430 --> 00:58:58,870
If we are students, he makes us lazy.

620
00:58:59,210 --> 00:59:03,300
And how much do we know him?

621
00:59:03,540 --> 00:59:07,590
How can we stay away from
his tricks?

622
00:59:08,560 --> 00:59:12,920
How can we destroy his might?

623
00:59:13,020 --> 00:59:20,770
To make the devil kneel and
destroy him...

624
00:59:21,380 --> 00:59:27,100
firstly, we will be good Muslims.

625
00:59:28,040 --> 00:59:30,300
Now, you say that...

626
00:59:31,000 --> 00:59:35,210
how will we be good Muslims?

627
00:59:36,980 --> 00:59:39,400
Our prophet says that...

628
00:59:40,530 --> 00:59:42,400
Peace be upon his name.

629
00:59:43,240 --> 00:59:45,110
A person who sees Allah
as the god...

630
00:59:46,020 --> 00:59:48,230
Islam as the religion...

631
00:59:48,550 --> 00:59:52,400
Muhammad as the prophet...

632
00:59:53,250 --> 01:00:00,480
has tasted the taste of faith.

633
01:00:00,810 --> 01:00:03,770
If we get the flavour of faith...

634
01:00:04,410 --> 01:00:08,930
then, we make the devil kneel.

635
01:00:11,240 --> 01:00:14,220
The one who tastes the flavour
of faith...

636
01:00:15,170 --> 01:00:19,280
will make Islam his priority.

637
01:00:19,440 --> 01:00:24,580
Islam is more important than
his position.

638
01:00:25,130 --> 01:00:28,080
More important than the spouse,
children...

639
01:00:28,570 --> 01:00:30,720
lover.

640
01:00:32,340 --> 01:00:42,140
Nothing in the world can keep him away
from the salaat.

641
01:00:43,150 --> 01:00:47,820
He won't forget to give alms.

642
01:00:48,440 --> 01:00:54,440
He won't be prideful for
sitting on a throne.

643
01:00:55,460 --> 01:00:58,980
If there are scholars who are
real Muslims in a country...

644
01:00:59,310 --> 01:01:02,530
science rears up there.

645
01:01:03,480 --> 01:01:06,010
If there are real judges...

646
01:01:06,740 --> 01:01:10,140
the country has justice too.

647
01:01:10,450 --> 01:01:13,530
If there are real merchants...

648
01:01:14,070 --> 01:01:17,590
that country prospers.

649
01:01:18,900 --> 01:01:23,200
We all mirror each other.

650
01:01:23,640 --> 01:01:25,690
What did our ancestors say?

651
01:01:26,580 --> 01:01:30,590
A rotten apple spoils the barrel.

652
01:01:31,200 --> 01:01:33,440
Allah's words say...

653
01:01:34,010 --> 01:01:42,220
Allah has didn't create two hearts
in one person's chest.

654
01:01:42,680 --> 01:01:52,420
If there aren't two hearts in one chest,
one Muslim shouldn't carry two loves.

655
01:01:54,280 --> 01:01:58,840
He shouldn't say that he is a Muslim
and commit adultery.

656
01:01:59,400 --> 01:02:03,490
He should protect the goods trusted
by the other.

657
01:02:04,020 --> 01:02:07,720
He should perform the salaat
rightly.

658
01:02:08,010 --> 01:02:10,720
He should give his alms.

659
01:02:11,540 --> 01:02:16,790
I hear it. Some people
neglect their salaat.

660
01:02:17,190 --> 01:02:22,830
Some people open their stores
without performing the morning salaat.

661
01:02:24,740 --> 01:02:27,520
My heart is burning.

662
01:02:28,310 --> 01:02:35,410
What kind of a Muslim am I that
my word doesn't work on you?

663
01:02:39,200 --> 01:02:40,560
I'm devastated.

664
01:02:42,720 --> 01:02:43,880
My dear ones.

665
01:02:44,920 --> 01:02:46,470
My Allah says...

666
01:02:46,990 --> 01:03:03,870
Who can speak better than the man who
calls people to the way of Allah?

667
01:03:09,680 --> 01:03:13,360
I am a Muslim.

668
01:03:15,870 --> 01:03:19,210
I am a Muslim.

669
01:03:21,420 --> 01:03:23,090
I am a Muslim.

670
01:03:23,250 --> 01:03:24,510
I am a Muslim.

671
01:03:25,140 --> 01:03:26,480
I am a Muslim.

672
01:03:26,580 --> 01:03:29,300
I am a Muslim.

673
01:03:30,170 --> 01:03:41,330
Then, may Allah destine us to become
real Muslims.

674
01:03:41,420 --> 01:03:43,220
Amin.

675
01:03:43,290 --> 01:03:45,610
Amin. Amin, my sheik.

676
01:03:45,610 --> 01:03:46,740
Amin.

677
01:03:47,860 --> 01:03:49,300
Amin.

678
01:03:54,420 --> 01:03:56,250
I'm tired.

679
01:03:57,140 --> 01:03:58,640
I'm tired.

680
01:03:59,280 --> 01:04:00,360
I'm hungry.

681
01:04:05,820 --> 01:04:06,570
A child.

682
01:04:10,170 --> 01:04:11,790
Did you forget your tent, child?

683
01:04:15,000 --> 01:04:17,280
And he is eating!

684
01:04:18,460 --> 01:04:22,360
If Aygül Hatun sees you, even I can't
save you.

685
01:04:25,560 --> 01:04:27,030
I hope you left some for me.

686
01:04:35,480 --> 01:04:38,180
He is sharing his bread with me!

687
01:04:38,890 --> 01:04:40,440
Are you hungry?

688
01:04:43,000 --> 01:04:44,720
Where are your parents?

689
01:04:47,180 --> 01:04:48,350
Who am I talking to?

690
01:04:48,810 --> 01:04:50,420
Did you gulp down your tongue?

691
01:04:53,610 --> 01:04:55,410
Slowly, slowly.

692
01:04:55,620 --> 01:04:57,190
Slowly.

693
01:04:57,300 --> 01:04:58,630
Open your mouth.

694
01:04:58,630 --> 01:05:00,920
Come on, it's coming!

695
01:05:01,630 --> 01:05:03,030
The basmala first!

696
01:05:03,410 --> 01:05:04,750
With Allah's name!

697
01:05:04,750 --> 01:05:06,160
Good job!

698
01:05:06,520 --> 01:05:08,280
This one. This one.

699
01:05:08,280 --> 01:05:09,180
We'll eat it.

700
01:05:09,280 --> 01:05:11,530
The horsemen are coming.

701
01:05:14,610 --> 01:05:17,480
Mashallah to my warrior!

702
01:05:17,580 --> 01:05:18,820
Mashallah!

703
01:05:18,820 --> 01:05:24,190
We'll use our spoons. Right hand,
right hand. Eat with your right hand.

704
01:05:24,190 --> 01:05:25,490
Mashallah.

705
01:05:26,280 --> 01:05:28,890
Mashallah to my warrior.

706
01:05:31,500 --> 01:05:34,370
Aygül Hatun. This warrior
lost his tent.

707
01:05:34,640 --> 01:05:37,040
He wanted to come to us.

708
01:05:37,690 --> 01:05:39,890
But he doesn't speak.
Just laugh.

709
01:05:46,300 --> 01:05:47,850
Why are you crying, mad girl?

710
01:05:49,180 --> 01:05:50,360
Nothing.

711
01:06:02,570 --> 01:06:03,680
Mother!

712
01:06:10,560 --> 01:06:14,040
Kayı. Cerkutay.

713
01:06:17,940 --> 01:06:19,330
Kayı?

714
01:06:22,770 --> 01:06:24,030
Baby Kayı?

715
01:06:25,870 --> 01:06:26,860
Baby Kayı?

716
01:06:27,510 --> 01:06:28,580
Baby Kayı?

717
01:06:30,370 --> 01:06:33,050
Mashallah to my warrior!

718
01:06:33,050 --> 01:06:35,790
You are a man now, Kayı!

719
01:06:36,060 --> 01:06:38,090
Welcome, Kayı!

720
01:06:41,910 --> 01:06:43,310
Welcome, Kayı.

721
01:06:53,840 --> 01:06:56,730
İnegöl Castle

722
01:07:03,390 --> 01:07:04,960
Michael Kosses.

723
01:07:06,070 --> 01:07:07,360
Aya Nikola.

724
01:07:07,640 --> 01:07:08,950
My dear friend.

725
01:07:10,530 --> 01:07:13,660
It's been a really long time.

726
01:07:13,660 --> 01:07:15,650
It has, Nikola.
It has.

727
01:07:16,290 --> 01:07:18,880
I wish it wasn't for something
like this.

728
01:07:19,810 --> 01:07:22,190
What is that, Nikola?

729
01:07:22,810 --> 01:07:23,990
Osman.

730
01:07:25,930 --> 01:07:33,500
If the lord of İnhisar stood with us
and helped against Osman...

731
01:07:34,170 --> 01:07:38,120
maybe this wouldn't
happen today.

732
01:07:38,360 --> 01:07:39,540
Of course.

733
01:07:40,800 --> 01:07:41,740
I mean...

734
01:07:42,200 --> 01:07:44,660
you shouldn't be waiting for the
fire...

735
01:07:44,660 --> 01:07:47,750
to spread to your house.

736
01:07:49,400 --> 01:07:50,500
Anyway.

737
01:07:50,720 --> 01:07:52,350
So, my friend.

738
01:07:52,350 --> 01:07:53,930
What can we do for you?

739
01:07:54,590 --> 01:07:55,690
Osman.

740
01:07:56,840 --> 01:07:58,490
He sent his man to my castle.

741
01:07:58,720 --> 01:08:00,390
He forced me into an agreement.

742
01:08:01,280 --> 01:08:04,530
You are like a vessel that has
the wind on its sails.

743
01:08:04,700 --> 01:08:07,750
I'll be the rock that will sink you.

744
01:08:08,640 --> 01:08:11,550
I need your help to
stand against Osman.

745
01:08:11,800 --> 01:08:12,660
Right away.

746
01:08:13,680 --> 01:08:17,439
I'll give my best soldiers to
you.

747
01:08:20,859 --> 01:08:24,220
I see that Osman won't stop, Nikola.

748
01:08:24,720 --> 01:08:26,779
Maybe if we don't unite now...

749
01:08:27,380 --> 01:08:30,540
no wall will stop him.

750
01:08:32,880 --> 01:08:35,210
Osman will break the treaty...

751
01:08:35,359 --> 01:08:38,300
and march to İnhisar first.

752
01:08:38,890 --> 01:08:41,939
Then, to İnegöl.

753
01:08:44,590 --> 01:08:46,770
Tomorrow, we'll be at the castle
with Nikola.

754
01:08:47,040 --> 01:08:49,979
And of course, Turgut will be with
us.

755
01:08:50,390 --> 01:08:51,380
Turgut?

756
01:08:52,620 --> 01:08:55,020
I don't want a Turk in my castle, Kosses.

757
01:08:59,040 --> 01:09:04,450
If we got rid of Geyhatu and the Vizier
thanks to Osman...

758
01:09:04,760 --> 01:09:10,100
we can get rid of Osman thanks to Turgut.

759
01:09:10,380 --> 01:09:12,920
Trust us.
This is how the Turks work.

760
01:09:13,080 --> 01:09:14,689
Use it and throw it.

761
01:09:14,779 --> 01:09:16,490
That's what we'll do.

762
01:09:17,250 --> 01:09:19,930
We'll use them and
throw them away.

763
01:09:22,000 --> 01:09:22,880
Alright.

764
01:09:24,880 --> 01:09:26,990
But it's your responsibility.

765
01:09:28,819 --> 01:09:30,240
I'll be waiting.

766
01:09:31,560 --> 01:09:32,760
I'm grateful.

767
01:09:32,939 --> 01:09:34,380
Lord Matheus.

768
01:09:44,000 --> 01:09:48,000
For revenge, Kosses, huh?

769
01:09:48,840 --> 01:09:53,920
You are after new alliances for revenge.

770
01:09:57,620 --> 01:10:00,850
What can I do?

771
01:10:01,700 --> 01:10:03,750
This is how revenge is.

772
01:10:04,440 --> 01:10:09,910
The revenge that made me Osman's
friend to destroy you...

773
01:10:11,080 --> 01:10:16,030
now making me Turgut's friend
to destroy Osman.

774
01:10:44,750 --> 01:10:46,110
My girl, are you alright?

775
01:10:47,500 --> 01:10:48,430
Cornelia?

776
01:10:48,720 --> 01:10:50,360
Cornelia?

777
01:10:51,910 --> 01:10:53,200
Cornelia, are you alright?

778
01:11:02,600 --> 01:11:05,370
She is poisoned! Mother, she is poisoned!

779
01:11:14,810 --> 01:11:16,400
Zehra!

780
01:11:20,480 --> 01:11:21,550
Zehra?

781
01:11:26,800 --> 01:11:27,730
My girl.

782
01:11:29,290 --> 01:11:31,040
Help me here.

783
01:11:31,040 --> 01:11:32,330
Puke it.

784
01:11:32,380 --> 01:11:34,660
Puke it.

785
01:11:40,020 --> 01:11:41,100
Come on, my girl.

786
01:11:54,890 --> 01:11:56,350
No.

787
01:12:01,020 --> 01:12:02,300
No.

788
01:12:09,600 --> 01:12:11,250
O' passanger!

789
01:12:14,520 --> 01:12:16,100
Where are you heading?

790
01:12:19,440 --> 01:12:21,060
To the Kızıl Elma!

791
01:12:35,360 --> 01:12:37,450
Have you seen Kosses' excitement, master?

792
01:12:37,450 --> 01:12:40,800
He was so eager to give soldiers
against Osman.

793
01:12:42,610 --> 01:12:45,230
You won't join Kosses' invitation, Nikola.

794
01:12:46,500 --> 01:12:50,540
Sure. But why?

795
01:12:51,280 --> 01:12:53,900
You are like a leave hanging
on the air.

796
01:12:53,900 --> 01:12:56,030
You follow the stream.

797
01:12:56,640 --> 01:12:59,040
Kosses was with Osman until yesterday.

798
01:12:59,310 --> 01:13:02,260
He can't gain my trust that easily.

799
01:13:03,430 --> 01:13:05,370
As you want, master.

800
01:13:06,260 --> 01:13:08,090
Don't forget this, Nikola.

801
01:13:08,810 --> 01:13:14,110
If the Turks don't have trouble,
they become the trouble.

802
01:13:15,050 --> 01:13:18,400
We are here to be their trouble.

803
01:13:19,250 --> 01:13:23,160
Yes, master.
What's our next move?

804
01:13:24,990 --> 01:13:26,010
Barkın.

805
01:13:28,480 --> 01:13:31,030
Barkın must take the tribes.

806
01:13:32,530 --> 01:13:34,800
Then, I'll take Osman's breath.

807
01:13:35,420 --> 01:13:37,730
I won't let him dream of conquests.

808
01:13:43,370 --> 01:13:48,640
Nikola asked for soldiers near Yenişehir
from the emperor.

809
01:13:52,070 --> 01:13:54,840
He is talking about the soldiers
Sultan Mesud will send.

810
01:13:56,040 --> 01:13:57,830
He wants to equalize the situtation.

811
01:13:59,160 --> 01:14:00,070
What else?

812
01:14:00,780 --> 01:14:05,080
And he demanded help against
a Turkish siege.

813
01:14:06,520 --> 01:14:09,220
Oil, mostly.

814
01:14:10,280 --> 01:14:11,620
Weasel.

815
01:14:12,290 --> 01:14:15,610
The helps to go to Nikola will
take this way.

816
01:14:17,370 --> 01:14:21,870
Cutting the supply will break
İnegöl's strenght.

817
01:14:29,680 --> 01:14:31,640
Tell me about Bursa.

818
01:14:33,020 --> 01:14:37,140
Bursa that you want to make
the capital of your country.

819
01:14:40,160 --> 01:14:42,360
The walls are hard to pass.

820
01:14:43,020 --> 01:14:45,880
Even stopping the supply line
will take years.

821
01:14:46,060 --> 01:14:47,880
Many villages are supporting it.

822
01:14:48,970 --> 01:14:52,640
The riches of it might be equal to
a hundred, maybe a thousand Söğüt.

823
01:14:55,070 --> 01:14:57,000
That's why we want it.

824
01:14:59,860 --> 01:15:02,250
It'll become our home.

825
01:15:02,590 --> 01:15:06,250
But, there is time.

826
01:15:09,380 --> 01:15:11,460
When we take İnhisar...

827
01:15:11,460 --> 01:15:15,160
we'll cut all the supplies coming
from the east.

828
01:15:17,510 --> 01:15:21,750
The rest is being cautious against
the ones coming from the west.

829
01:15:22,470 --> 01:15:26,600
If your relative, emperor Andrenikos
heard this...

830
01:15:30,240 --> 01:15:33,400
If my relative, emperor Andrenikos...

831
01:15:33,530 --> 01:15:37,210
heard the information you
bring to us?

832
01:15:40,910 --> 01:15:42,290
Artholos.

833
01:15:43,080 --> 01:15:46,300
We know that İnhisar isn't enough
to conquer İnegöl.

834
01:15:49,650 --> 01:15:54,100
But the important part, who'll fill
Rogatus' place?

835
01:15:55,060 --> 01:15:59,510
The new lord of Bilecik, whose
side will he be on?

836
01:16:01,760 --> 01:16:03,990
There are some names rumored.

837
01:16:04,780 --> 01:16:08,720
I'll inform Osman Bey when it's
certain.

838
01:16:11,310 --> 01:16:13,390
You'll bring the information.

839
01:16:14,380 --> 01:16:18,130
I'll bring the soldiers.
All the alps.

840
01:16:21,620 --> 01:16:25,970
Kosses and Turgut Bey will stand with me.

841
01:16:31,180 --> 01:16:35,550
First, İnhisar...

842
01:16:38,950 --> 01:16:39,750
İnegöl...

843
01:16:42,670 --> 01:16:43,880
Bilecik.

844
01:16:48,710 --> 01:16:49,860
İznik.

845
01:16:50,870 --> 01:16:51,990
And...

846
01:16:56,080 --> 01:16:57,700
Bursa.

847
01:17:18,160 --> 01:17:20,100
Children will be raised.

848
01:17:21,880 --> 01:17:23,630
Causes will grow.

849
01:17:25,450 --> 01:17:31,050
This nation that is loyal to a dream,
the idea of world order...

850
01:17:32,100 --> 01:17:37,420
will conquest Constantinople
one day...

851
01:17:38,900 --> 01:17:40,740
and make it home.

852
01:17:42,040 --> 01:17:43,300
Alright.

853
01:17:47,380 --> 01:17:50,910
All people deserve prosperity and peace.

854
01:17:52,200 --> 01:17:53,500
The most importantly...

855
01:17:53,890 --> 01:17:57,940
these lands will live in peace.

856
01:18:01,500 --> 01:18:04,210
These lands will be ruled with
justice.

857
01:18:06,670 --> 01:18:09,940
Intelligence is crucial in winning
a war.

858
01:18:11,210 --> 01:18:13,550
And you keep the key, Osman Bey.

859
01:18:15,260 --> 01:18:17,360
The key to conquest is the heart.

860
01:18:18,430 --> 01:18:20,760
The rest is just tools.

861
01:18:25,530 --> 01:18:30,230
They think that they divided us.
Finished us.

862
01:18:30,540 --> 01:18:31,840
But...

863
01:18:34,150 --> 01:18:36,120
thank Allah.

864
01:18:38,370 --> 01:18:40,110
We haven't started yet.

865
01:18:43,640 --> 01:18:47,600
Now, it's time for conquest.

866
01:18:49,500 --> 01:18:51,120
Allahu Akbar.

867
01:18:52,550 --> 01:18:54,660
Allahu Akbar.

868
01:18:57,930 --> 01:18:59,120
Alright.

869
01:19:04,900 --> 01:19:07,000
Bring water.

870
01:19:07,190 --> 01:19:10,230
Alaca, go to the infirmary and
bring what I said.

871
01:19:16,390 --> 01:19:18,240
Come on!
Come on!

872
01:19:22,940 --> 01:19:24,980
Come on, my girl.

873
01:19:24,980 --> 01:19:26,180
Alps!

874
01:19:29,490 --> 01:19:31,530
Take Zehra to the prisoner tent!

875
01:19:33,950 --> 01:19:35,660
And inform Kumral Abdal.

876
01:19:36,020 --> 01:19:37,050
Bala Hatun.

877
01:19:38,050 --> 01:19:41,710
Bala Hatun! I didn't do it!
I didn't do it!

878
01:19:41,710 --> 01:19:43,630
I didn't hurt anyone.

879
01:19:43,660 --> 01:19:47,250
Bala Hatun! Bala Hatun!

880
01:19:56,070 --> 01:19:57,840
What kind of a tribe is this?

881
01:19:58,040 --> 01:20:00,200
The troubles and traitors
never end!

882
01:20:00,440 --> 01:20:03,310
Selda Hatun, know your words.

883
01:20:09,150 --> 01:20:11,080
We came for condolences.

884
01:20:11,410 --> 01:20:13,320
Is it a bad time?

885
01:20:13,340 --> 01:20:15,270
You are just in time, İbrahim Fakih.

886
01:20:15,270 --> 01:20:17,040
Cornelia is poisoned now!

887
01:20:25,350 --> 01:20:28,120
It's the same with Sheik Edebali's
poison.

888
01:20:49,400 --> 01:20:50,230
Beys.

889
01:20:51,380 --> 01:20:52,080
I know.

890
01:20:53,530 --> 01:20:57,350
You are asking why we are here.

891
01:20:58,580 --> 01:21:00,620
It's important matter.

892
01:21:02,020 --> 01:21:06,130
Walls have ears in Kayı Tribe.

893
01:21:06,320 --> 01:21:10,170
As the Kızılbeyoğlu Tribe,
we've been with Osman Bey.

894
01:21:10,170 --> 01:21:11,460
It's Umur Bey's will.

895
01:21:11,880 --> 01:21:14,770
So, say it now.

896
01:21:17,800 --> 01:21:24,810
Umur Bey and İhvaz Bey both died
on their way to Osman Bey.

897
01:21:26,110 --> 01:21:30,510
I'm here by their will and wish.

898
01:21:33,140 --> 01:21:34,020
Tell me.

899
01:21:35,900 --> 01:21:37,550
Why were they on the way?

900
01:21:40,400 --> 01:21:42,520
For the future of the Turks.

901
01:21:43,100 --> 01:21:45,160
To reach the Kızıl Elma.

902
01:21:45,500 --> 01:21:46,940
Now, I ask you.

903
01:21:48,940 --> 01:21:51,610
One who can't keep his own
roads safe...

904
01:21:54,570 --> 01:21:57,090
how can he open the way
to the Kızıl Elma?

905
01:21:57,400 --> 01:22:01,450
Barkın Bey. You were with Umur Bey
when he died.

906
01:22:02,410 --> 01:22:05,680
Will the man who can't protect his bey
will be our bey?

907
01:22:07,850 --> 01:22:09,300
You are right?

908
01:22:11,350 --> 01:22:13,010
I couldn't protect them.

909
01:22:15,040 --> 01:22:17,080
And I couldn't die.

910
01:22:18,650 --> 01:22:19,740
But...

911
01:22:21,780 --> 01:22:23,360
Allah is my witness that...

912
01:22:25,300 --> 01:22:27,510
I didn't step back from a fight...

913
01:22:29,050 --> 01:22:30,850
or turn my back.

914
01:22:36,370 --> 01:22:38,850
I fought bravely and couldn't protect him.

915
01:22:42,030 --> 01:22:43,840
And it's my shame.

916
01:22:44,190 --> 01:22:48,330
We have many martyrs!

917
01:22:48,740 --> 01:22:50,850
Are you questioning everyone
who survives?

918
01:22:52,250 --> 01:22:53,770
Continue, Barkın Bey.

919
01:22:58,120 --> 01:23:00,810
Söğüt is the heart of the Kayı.

920
01:23:01,060 --> 01:23:02,810
He can't even protect it.

921
01:23:04,030 --> 01:23:08,620
We came here to protect
the borders...

922
01:23:08,620 --> 01:23:11,790
to run for one battle
after another.

923
01:23:12,800 --> 01:23:18,230
We won't bow down to Osman Bey
just because our beys are gone.

924
01:23:19,220 --> 01:23:21,550
If we need a bey...

925
01:23:24,180 --> 01:23:25,720
it can be me.

926
01:23:54,020 --> 01:23:56,460
I'm poor.

927
01:24:06,920 --> 01:24:08,050
But...

928
01:24:11,200 --> 01:24:13,430
my tribe will prosper.

929
01:24:33,850 --> 01:24:36,280
May Allah bless you, İbrahim Fakih.

930
01:24:36,910 --> 01:24:38,000
Thank Allah.

931
01:24:41,320 --> 01:24:42,980
She breaths again.

932
01:24:47,150 --> 01:24:48,480
Give this to her.

933
01:24:51,260 --> 01:24:55,580
Allah is the one healing.
We are just tools.

934
01:25:05,210 --> 01:25:08,500
Mashallah. You understand it
with a single look.

935
01:25:09,680 --> 01:25:12,170
You are pretty informed on this.

936
01:25:14,020 --> 01:25:16,550
Science is knowing the nature.

937
01:25:16,550 --> 01:25:19,100
Poison is a part of it.

938
01:25:19,560 --> 01:25:21,860
We are educated on it too.

939
01:25:21,860 --> 01:25:23,150
Thank Allah.

940
01:25:28,300 --> 01:25:29,480
Firstly, my sheik...

941
01:25:30,360 --> 01:25:31,680
now Cornelia.

942
01:25:35,140 --> 01:25:36,900
How will we pay our debt?

943
01:25:38,240 --> 01:25:40,100
Stay in our tribe today.

944
01:25:40,100 --> 01:25:40,940
Don't travel.

945
01:25:41,420 --> 01:25:43,320
Osman Bey will come too.

946
01:25:46,440 --> 01:25:48,360
He'll want to see you.

947
01:25:56,160 --> 01:25:57,300
İbrahim Fakih.

948
01:25:58,060 --> 01:25:59,160
Osman Bey.

949
01:26:04,740 --> 01:26:06,700
I owed you a life.

950
01:26:16,440 --> 01:26:17,640
Now it's two.

951
01:26:20,480 --> 01:26:22,280
Come to my tent for dinner.

952
01:26:23,000 --> 01:26:27,020
Thank you, Osman Bey.
But it was a tiring day.

953
01:26:27,780 --> 01:26:30,720
Forgive me for tonight.

954
01:26:53,440 --> 01:26:56,605
Cornelia is the last to see Mari.
She brought the food to the lodge

955
01:26:56,955 --> 01:26:58,860
We suspected her.

956
01:26:59,140 --> 01:27:01,360
But Cornelia is poisoned now, my bey.

957
01:27:02,580 --> 01:27:04,640
The traitor was one of us.

958
01:27:07,600 --> 01:27:09,780
Zehra has no one.

959
01:27:10,760 --> 01:27:13,180
Who would make her do this?

960
01:27:15,180 --> 01:27:16,940
We'll make her speak.

961
01:27:18,240 --> 01:27:19,940
What do you think, mother?

962
01:27:20,820 --> 01:27:23,920
Until now, I always suspected
Cornelia, son.

963
01:27:24,780 --> 01:27:26,480
But now I'm sure.

964
01:27:26,600 --> 01:27:28,740
It was Cornelia.

965
01:27:29,400 --> 01:27:32,100
She told Bala that she didn't
touch the meal.

966
01:27:32,560 --> 01:27:35,040
But she put the meal on the bowl.

967
01:27:37,540 --> 01:27:39,940
Oh, my Ayşe.

968
01:27:39,940 --> 01:27:42,320
And she got the meal
from Ayşe.

969
01:27:43,740 --> 01:27:48,620
When she realized that Bala suspected
her, she poisoned herself.

970
01:27:51,660 --> 01:27:54,000
Do you say that she risked death?

971
01:27:54,800 --> 01:27:56,820
She struggled in front of our eyes.

972
01:28:00,080 --> 01:28:02,660
She would.
She would.

973
01:28:04,240 --> 01:28:07,280
And again, İbrahim Fakih came.

974
01:28:11,560 --> 01:28:13,800
Every time we are in trouble...

975
01:28:15,660 --> 01:28:17,740
İbrahim Fakih comes in time

976
01:28:20,580 --> 01:28:22,400
Oh, my son.
Oh...

977
01:28:22,820 --> 01:28:24,320
Have you seen it?

978
01:28:25,220 --> 01:28:26,800
Your brother is innocent.

979
01:28:28,440 --> 01:28:30,440
My children died for nothing.

980
01:28:35,120 --> 01:28:36,020
Mother.

981
01:28:37,000 --> 01:28:39,360
I couldn't tell you.
Forgive me.

982
01:28:40,580 --> 01:28:41,380
What?

983
01:28:43,060 --> 01:28:45,260
Gündüz Bey and Ayşe Hatun
are safe and sound.

984
01:28:46,520 --> 01:28:49,440
Thank Allah!

985
01:28:51,120 --> 01:28:52,640
Thank Allah!

986
01:28:53,360 --> 01:28:54,500
Thank Allah!

987
01:28:59,100 --> 01:29:01,000
No one will hear it.

988
01:29:01,920 --> 01:29:03,790
The enemies attack from the shadows.

989
01:29:04,760 --> 01:29:06,860
We'll fight them secretly.

990
01:29:07,140 --> 01:29:09,840
Only the alps and you.

991
01:29:18,700 --> 01:29:21,260
Bala, we need the one
who holds the leashes.

992
01:29:21,860 --> 01:29:24,000
But still question Zehra Hatun.

993
01:29:25,040 --> 01:29:26,580
Don't worry, my bey.

994
01:29:31,180 --> 01:29:33,080
May I enter, my bey?

995
01:29:33,580 --> 01:29:35,080
Come, Cerkutay.

996
01:29:42,620 --> 01:29:44,400
Oh, my nephew is here!

997
01:29:52,880 --> 01:29:54,980
Come here, my lion!

998
01:29:55,600 --> 01:29:56,760
Come here!

999
01:29:59,380 --> 01:30:00,540
Kayı Alp!

1000
01:30:01,320 --> 01:30:03,900
You are a soldier!

1001
01:30:03,900 --> 01:30:05,900
Mashallah to you!

1002
01:30:10,600 --> 01:30:12,160
Mashallah!

1003
01:30:16,380 --> 01:30:18,200
My lion.

1004
01:30:20,860 --> 01:30:23,540
He would grow bigger if
had sleept.

1005
01:30:28,460 --> 01:30:30,180
What did I tell you, Cerkutay?

1006
01:30:31,280 --> 01:30:32,680
He should sleep.

1007
01:30:34,360 --> 01:30:35,380
Why didn't he sleep?

1008
01:30:37,760 --> 01:30:40,460
He didn't, mad girl!
He didn't!

1009
01:30:40,860 --> 01:30:43,010
He burned the tent by
shouting 'mother'!

1010
01:30:46,040 --> 01:30:49,380
Mashallah to my valiant.

1011
01:30:51,660 --> 01:30:55,280
Did you shout 'mother', Kayı?

1012
01:31:13,300 --> 01:31:15,740
Coins don't work on them.

1013
01:31:16,780 --> 01:31:19,940
Poverty doesn't disband them.

1014
01:31:22,040 --> 01:31:23,900
Why did we give the coins, then?

1015
01:31:24,260 --> 01:31:25,180
Barkın.

1016
01:31:27,040 --> 01:31:30,000
We did it to show off.

1017
01:31:30,500 --> 01:31:35,660
This was the show off of a bey
who doesn't care about money.

1018
01:31:36,300 --> 01:31:40,300
It shows that you will never be
arrogant.

1019
01:31:41,380 --> 01:31:43,360
You will give promises, Barkın.

1020
01:31:44,780 --> 01:31:48,280
You will give them a dream.

1021
01:31:48,840 --> 01:31:52,720
They will sleep and wake up
with that dream.

1022
01:31:53,820 --> 01:31:57,340
They like peace.

1023
01:31:59,620 --> 01:32:03,700
They like unity.

1024
01:32:04,300 --> 01:32:11,500
But they know that it's all possible
through destroying the heathens.

1025
01:32:12,340 --> 01:32:14,080
For that, Barkın...

1026
01:32:15,160 --> 01:32:17,580
you will promise them raids.

1027
01:32:18,220 --> 01:32:19,400
Raids.

1028
01:32:21,860 --> 01:32:23,500
That's our weakness.

1029
01:32:25,960 --> 01:32:28,600
You'll hit them on their
weak points.

1030
01:32:35,660 --> 01:32:38,920
It seems like Barkın is busy.

1031
01:32:39,320 --> 01:32:42,080
What are they talking about?

1032
01:32:42,460 --> 01:32:44,800
We don't know their deal but...

1033
01:32:45,940 --> 01:32:47,620
we keep our eyes on them.

1034
01:32:48,980 --> 01:32:50,540
We'll find out.

1035
01:32:55,540 --> 01:32:56,760
Alps!

1036
01:32:58,320 --> 01:33:00,380
This road leads to İnhisar.

1037
01:33:01,220 --> 01:33:07,480
But the other side of the walls doesn't
only contain İnhisar!

1038
01:33:08,140 --> 01:33:11,780
Behind those walls, there is İnegöl!

1039
01:33:13,640 --> 01:33:16,080
Yesterday, we had Geyhatu and
Alemşah...

1040
01:33:16,600 --> 01:33:19,740
tomorrow we have other enemies.

1041
01:33:21,220 --> 01:33:22,260
It seems that...

1042
01:33:23,680 --> 01:33:26,560
as long as we don't become
a state...

1043
01:33:27,480 --> 01:33:30,220
they'll try to stop us.

1044
01:33:33,660 --> 01:33:35,240
Now, it's time.

1045
01:33:35,900 --> 01:33:38,940
It's time for conquests!

1046
01:33:38,940 --> 01:33:53,900
Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

1047
01:34:15,700 --> 01:34:17,920
Ya Allah!

1048
01:34:22,640 --> 01:34:23,580
Barkın Bey.

1049
01:34:23,980 --> 01:34:25,280
You are here.

1050
01:34:26,080 --> 01:34:28,060
Selvi Hatun is here.

1051
01:34:28,500 --> 01:34:30,820
Where is Umur Bey's daughter,
Malhun Hatun?

1052
01:34:32,820 --> 01:34:34,160
Malhun Hatun is resting.

1053
01:34:35,160 --> 01:34:36,760
If she felt well...

1054
01:34:36,760 --> 01:34:38,760
she would be among us.

1055
01:34:39,220 --> 01:34:42,000
Will we elect Umur Bey's
tribe's head without his daughter?

1056
01:34:42,000 --> 01:34:44,000
His brother İhvaz Bey's daughter
is here.

1057
01:34:44,420 --> 01:34:45,860
Isn't it enough?

1058
01:34:52,560 --> 01:34:53,760
Now.

1059
01:34:54,340 --> 01:34:58,740
I want to be the bey
of the both tribes.

1060
01:34:59,800 --> 01:35:04,200
I see that there is no one else
who wants it.

1061
01:35:06,360 --> 01:35:11,560
So, to honor our laws, we
are gathering a council here.

1062
01:35:11,960 --> 01:35:13,040
He isn't facing you.

1063
01:35:14,020 --> 01:35:16,150
He is busy with more
important things.

1064
01:35:17,140 --> 01:35:19,160
But you have competitors, Barkın Bey.

1065
01:35:22,420 --> 01:35:23,560
Speak.

1066
01:35:24,460 --> 01:35:25,440
Who is it?

1067
01:35:26,600 --> 01:35:28,020
Osman Bey!

1068
01:35:29,280 --> 01:35:31,760
Malhun Hatun is Osman Bey's wife.

1069
01:35:32,540 --> 01:35:34,720
Umur Bey left her to us.

1070
01:35:36,800 --> 01:35:43,200
So, we want to follow Osman Bey.

1071
01:35:48,800 --> 01:35:50,200
And these are your coins.

1072
01:35:50,200 --> 01:35:51,270
Come on.

1073
01:35:51,400 --> 01:35:52,200
Hasan Bey!

1074
01:36:13,700 --> 01:36:16,800
Are you afraid of me?

1075
01:36:17,120 --> 01:36:19,060
I'm not, Barkın Bey!

1076
01:36:22,620 --> 01:36:24,040
Yes.

1077
01:36:27,420 --> 01:36:28,300
Yes.

1078
01:36:31,000 --> 01:36:31,940
But...

1079
01:36:33,440 --> 01:36:35,480
you are afraid of Osman Bey.

1080
01:36:39,180 --> 01:36:42,880
You are afraid of facing him.

1081
01:36:44,440 --> 01:36:49,600
One who cares about his tribe
wouldn't follow another!

1082
01:36:51,480 --> 01:36:55,820
I rode my horse for
the safety of the borders.

1083
01:36:57,860 --> 01:37:00,120
I joined battles!

1084
01:37:01,100 --> 01:37:02,880
I lost my alps.

1085
01:37:06,700 --> 01:37:07,860
Hasan Bey!

1086
01:37:09,080 --> 01:37:12,000
I didn't give the coins to you
that you can reject them.

1087
01:37:13,680 --> 01:37:17,960
I gave them to the poor in your
tribe to be happy.

1088
01:37:20,900 --> 01:37:25,600
It's obvious that you don't
care about your people.

1089
01:37:27,960 --> 01:37:30,700
Now, I ask you.
Beys.

1090
01:37:40,960 --> 01:37:47,940
Do you want Osman Bey, who is incapable
of protecting his own, as your leader?

1091
01:37:49,280 --> 01:37:55,620
Or Barkın Bey who risks his own life
for your safety?

1092
01:38:00,360 --> 01:38:01,780
Tell me.

1093
01:38:02,400 --> 01:38:04,300
We vote for Barkın Bey.

1094
01:38:04,920 --> 01:38:06,820
I also vote for Barkın Bey.

1095
01:38:07,480 --> 01:38:09,360
I also vote for Barkın Bey.

1096
01:38:13,180 --> 01:38:17,740
Hasan Bey, İhvaz Bey chose Barkın
Bey to be his son-in-law.

1097
01:38:19,080 --> 01:38:20,760
He saw the truth.

1098
01:38:22,500 --> 01:38:23,940
I vote for Barkın Bey.

1099
01:38:24,380 --> 01:38:26,020
Thank you.

1100
01:38:30,260 --> 01:38:31,980
I vote for Barkın Bey.

1101
01:38:43,440 --> 01:38:46,480
İnhisar Castle

1102
01:38:48,320 --> 01:38:50,900
I'm sorry for your sister, Lod Kosses.

1103
01:38:52,440 --> 01:38:56,080
But she prepared her end by
marrying a Turk.

1104
01:38:59,380 --> 01:39:02,960
I took my sister's revenge.

1105
01:39:03,380 --> 01:39:04,620
Lord Matheus.

1106
01:39:06,640 --> 01:39:10,200
I sent Osman's brother to hell.

1107
01:39:11,200 --> 01:39:14,340
But if you say such a thing again...

1108
01:39:14,720 --> 01:39:17,480
you will go and see him there.

1109
01:39:18,580 --> 01:39:21,220
Alright. Are you feeling peaceful now?

1110
01:39:22,680 --> 01:39:27,900
To feel peaceful, I need to kill
all those Turks, Matheus.

1111
01:39:28,540 --> 01:39:31,580
Don't worry.
I know how to do that.

1112
01:39:32,240 --> 01:39:34,500
Turgut will join us soon.

1113
01:39:35,500 --> 01:39:38,140
He wants to take revenge too.

1114
01:39:38,840 --> 01:39:42,080
Don't say such things with him.

1115
01:39:42,540 --> 01:39:46,540
Allow me to choose my own words
in my own castle.

1116
01:39:47,720 --> 01:39:49,820
Just as I choose my own alliances.

1117
01:39:54,200 --> 01:39:57,640
Isn't this a lot of soldiers, Matheus?

1118
01:39:58,020 --> 01:39:59,120
Why?

1119
01:39:59,580 --> 01:40:00,920
I'm hosting a Turk.

1120
01:40:02,360 --> 01:40:03,720
This is little.

1121
01:40:09,124 --> 01:40:11,204
Sir, they are coming.

1122
01:40:20,760 --> 01:40:23,070
I congratulate your beyhood, Barkın bey.

1123
01:40:24,550 --> 01:40:28,130
I hope it will be good.

1124
01:40:28,510 --> 01:40:29,430
Inshallah.

1125
01:40:30,050 --> 01:40:32,530
Soon, we'll host a festival.

1126
01:40:33,780 --> 01:40:35,110
If we are chosen the bey...

1127
01:40:35,310 --> 01:40:37,940
it's not to oppose Osman Bey
but to support him.

1128
01:40:38,510 --> 01:40:40,260
After we survive
these troubles...

1129
01:40:40,350 --> 01:40:44,410
we'll host our festival too.

1130
01:40:46,240 --> 01:40:47,220
Thank you.

1131
01:41:16,160 --> 01:41:19,840
Here is Turgut Bey, Lord Matheus.

1132
01:41:20,710 --> 01:41:23,100
You are the first Turk to eat
in my castle.

1133
01:41:23,800 --> 01:41:27,040
Inshallah, many more will eat in
your castle.

1134
01:41:29,450 --> 01:41:32,510
I'm talking about friendship.

1135
01:41:35,500 --> 01:41:37,380
Will he sit with us?

1136
01:41:38,940 --> 01:41:42,410
That's my brother.
He will stand behind me!

1137
01:41:42,500 --> 01:41:44,630
Of course.
Of course.

1138
01:41:46,420 --> 01:41:48,770
If it's not a trouble for you, Matheus.

1139
01:41:48,840 --> 01:41:52,160
As long as he is standing and
stays away from me.

1140
01:41:54,650 --> 01:41:55,960
Let's get to the table.

1141
01:42:07,360 --> 01:42:09,930
Lord Kosses' soldiers.
You are late.

1142
01:42:09,990 --> 01:42:12,270
We followed Lord Kosses' orders.

1143
01:42:12,910 --> 01:42:13,840
Wait here.

1144
01:42:28,740 --> 01:42:31,030
Nikola should be here soon.

1145
01:42:32,200 --> 01:42:33,940
Nikola isn't usually late.

1146
01:42:35,000 --> 01:42:36,180
Let's wait for a little
longer.

1147
01:42:41,630 --> 01:42:45,960
The help we expect from the emperor
will come this way.

1148
01:42:47,430 --> 01:42:49,480
Soldiers, Argus.

1149
01:42:51,410 --> 01:42:54,280
Did the soldiers go to
guard them?

1150
01:42:54,350 --> 01:42:55,280
Yes, sir.

1151
01:42:55,890 --> 01:42:57,930
Our soldiers are providing
their security.

1152
01:42:59,270 --> 01:43:00,050
Good.

1153
01:43:01,230 --> 01:43:02,890
Good, Argus.

1154
01:43:03,550 --> 01:43:05,790
Our oil is coming.

1155
01:43:06,800 --> 01:43:09,240
Our walls are getting stronger.

1156
01:43:10,150 --> 01:43:12,670
But most importantly...

1157
01:43:13,190 --> 01:43:18,090
we have enough supplies for
years.

1158
01:43:18,750 --> 01:43:24,520
But, will it be enough?
No.

1159
01:43:26,480 --> 01:43:28,440
The best defense...

1160
01:43:30,890 --> 01:43:33,040
is offense.

1161
01:43:33,270 --> 01:43:34,990
What is our target, sir?

1162
01:43:41,370 --> 01:43:43,660
Prepare the soldiers.

1163
01:43:45,660 --> 01:43:47,830
We are charging.

1164
01:43:48,170 --> 01:43:49,630
Yes, sir.

1165
01:43:55,340 --> 01:43:58,060
Did you witness it?

1166
01:43:58,380 --> 01:44:00,060
We have.

1167
01:44:02,920 --> 01:44:05,690
May Allah make it good.

1168
01:44:10,600 --> 01:44:11,470
My Allah...

1169
01:44:14,700 --> 01:44:18,180
We witnessed the treaty of these
children of ours.

1170
01:44:18,360 --> 01:44:19,930
You witness it too.

1171
01:44:20,720 --> 01:44:23,090
May Allah bless this union.

1172
01:44:23,090 --> 01:44:25,090
Amin.

1173
01:44:25,820 --> 01:44:32,500
Give them prosperity, love, and peace
in their marriage.

1174
01:44:32,900 --> 01:44:34,360
-Amin.
-Amin.

1175
01:44:35,440 --> 01:44:40,640
Don't give them any discord, hate,
seperation.

1176
01:44:41,170 --> 01:44:42,020
Amin.

1177
01:44:44,280 --> 01:44:45,150
Amin.

1178
01:44:54,790 --> 01:44:56,010
Lord Kosses.

1179
01:44:56,880 --> 01:44:59,030
You will protect me against Osman,
won't you?

1180
01:45:02,630 --> 01:45:04,290
Lord Matheus.

1181
01:45:04,290 --> 01:45:07,080
I think you are overestimating Osman.

1182
01:45:07,330 --> 01:45:12,270
Kosses is right. Osman is rotting
his life after a dream.

1183
01:45:14,360 --> 01:45:17,460
For our friendship and unity.

1184
01:45:26,720 --> 01:45:29,430
If we are friends.
Let me give you some advice.

1185
01:45:31,650 --> 01:45:36,330
If you want to beat your enemy.
You should get to know him.

1186
01:45:38,140 --> 01:45:41,510
Tell me about Osman's
dream, then.

1187
01:45:42,090 --> 01:45:43,270
Let me tell you.

1188
01:45:44,340 --> 01:45:50,060
Osman wants to stop all the tyrants,
all over the world.

1189
01:45:53,570 --> 01:45:56,940
For this reason, he wants to
control the world.

1190
01:45:59,430 --> 01:46:00,800
What a dream.

1191
01:46:06,730 --> 01:46:08,950
Are you one of the tyrants?

1192
01:46:10,040 --> 01:46:11,750
Your people don't like you.

1193
01:46:12,580 --> 01:46:15,140
You oppress them with
heavy taxes.

1194
01:46:17,320 --> 01:46:19,070
My people, my rules.

1195
01:46:19,680 --> 01:46:21,940
It's not your concern, Turgut Bey.

1196
01:46:22,410 --> 01:46:24,150
Because you think like that...

1197
01:46:27,210 --> 01:46:29,050
it concerns Osman Bey.

1198
01:46:30,970 --> 01:46:32,510
Salam Alaikum.

1199
01:46:37,180 --> 01:46:39,610
Magneficus!

1200
01:46:44,510 --> 01:46:47,800
Traitors! You took Osman
to my castle.

1201
01:46:47,800 --> 01:46:50,750
But you were too naive, Matheus.

1202
01:46:51,120 --> 01:46:52,750
We heard it, Matheus.

1203
01:46:53,790 --> 01:46:58,200
You ruled as a tyrant.

1204
01:46:58,670 --> 01:47:02,950
But we came here with the
sword of justice.

1205
01:47:05,190 --> 01:47:12,870
Now, İnhisar belongs to the Kayı,
to the Turks, to Islam!

1206
01:48:25,640 --> 01:48:29,150
Give the treasury to the people,
Turgut Bey.

1207
01:48:29,800 --> 01:48:31,840
You'll gain the people's hearts.

1208
01:48:32,120 --> 01:48:34,750
And they'll hear that you took the castle.

1209
01:48:34,750 --> 01:48:37,100
The people will be ruled justly now.

1210
01:48:38,020 --> 01:48:39,290
Thank you, Osman Bey.

1211
01:48:42,170 --> 01:48:46,890
So, Osman Bey. İnegöl is next.

1212
01:48:47,970 --> 01:48:50,370
Nikola must be prepared.

1213
01:48:52,690 --> 01:48:54,950
It won't be easy to take İnegöl.

1214
01:48:56,630 --> 01:48:58,410
But we'll do it.

1215
01:49:02,460 --> 01:49:06,470
Share the treasury between the alps
and the people.

1216
01:49:07,370 --> 01:49:10,240
Alps will get their spoils!

1217
01:49:10,850 --> 01:49:13,030
And encouraged by the
spirit of conquest.

1218
01:49:13,390 --> 01:49:14,520
Alright.

1219
01:49:15,400 --> 01:49:17,550
The target is İnegöl now!

1220
01:49:51,640 --> 01:49:54,090
The antidote is working.

1221
01:49:54,090 --> 01:49:57,520
With Allah's help, you'll be
on your feet soon.

1222
01:49:59,760 --> 01:50:01,460
Thank you, master.

1223
01:50:04,190 --> 01:50:06,100
I owe you a life.

1224
01:50:20,000 --> 01:50:21,000
Alaca.

1225
01:50:21,760 --> 01:50:24,240
Can you give me water?

1226
01:50:28,520 --> 01:50:30,380
It's empty. I'll be back.

1227
01:50:44,820 --> 01:50:46,840
My enduring Cornelia.

1228
01:50:46,840 --> 01:50:48,840
Are you any better?

1229
01:50:49,480 --> 01:50:51,060
Thanks to you.

1230
01:51:00,720 --> 01:51:01,600
Alaca.

1231
01:51:02,000 --> 01:51:03,760
Come with me outside.

1232
01:51:28,960 --> 01:51:30,840
Now, listen to me carefully.

1233
01:51:32,540 --> 01:51:35,020
You'll keep your eyes
on Cornelia.

1234
01:51:35,700 --> 01:51:38,540
You'll inform me if you
see anything wrong.

1235
01:51:39,220 --> 01:51:40,540
What is it, Mother Selcan?

1236
01:51:42,360 --> 01:51:43,840
It's, my girl...

1237
01:51:44,560 --> 01:51:47,800
I don't believe that Zehra
would do this treachery.

1238
01:52:03,780 --> 01:52:07,340
Selcan still suspects me.

1239
01:52:09,460 --> 01:52:12,440
That old woman is too smart.

1240
01:52:14,660 --> 01:52:16,080
She might be a problem.

1241
01:52:19,780 --> 01:52:23,380
We'll make sure she can't
question you.

1242
01:52:33,200 --> 01:52:38,260
Barkın Bey's coins changed the
way of your heart.

1243
01:52:41,120 --> 01:52:43,340
You used your vote for him.

1244
01:52:43,800 --> 01:52:45,000
I have, my bey.

1245
01:52:45,320 --> 01:52:46,880
When the beys voted for him.

1246
01:52:49,880 --> 01:52:52,960
She is gossipping my bey
like crones.

1247
01:52:53,040 --> 01:52:54,460
No.

1248
01:52:54,460 --> 01:52:56,760
Not like that, Malhun Hatun.

1249
01:52:57,280 --> 01:53:00,260
Barkın Bey respects you.

1250
01:53:00,620 --> 01:53:04,920
The recent events affected him,
apparently.

1251
01:53:05,980 --> 01:53:06,820
My bey.

1252
01:53:08,360 --> 01:53:11,500
Hasan Bey speaks softly.

1253
01:53:12,760 --> 01:53:14,780
He is afraid to speak fully.

1254
01:53:16,180 --> 01:53:18,800
He can't openly say that Barkın Bey
was out of his way.

1255
01:53:20,860 --> 01:53:24,280
Everyone will be ruled as
they deserve.

1256
01:53:27,000 --> 01:53:28,100
Hasan Bey.

1257
01:53:29,540 --> 01:53:33,900
If you voted. You'll face
the consequences.

1258
01:53:36,980 --> 01:53:38,790
You are allowed to leave.

1259
01:53:46,160 --> 01:53:48,880
Hasan Bey voted Barkın Bey because
he had to.

1260
01:53:49,860 --> 01:53:50,780
He is one of us.

1261
01:53:54,620 --> 01:53:55,540
Protect him.

1262
01:53:56,140 --> 01:53:57,920
As you order, my bey.

1263
01:54:00,600 --> 01:54:02,780
Still, he didn't stand against him.

1264
01:54:03,760 --> 01:54:05,520
He voted for Barkın.

1265
01:54:06,100 --> 01:54:08,470
How did you come to
this conclusion, Osman?

1266
01:54:10,800 --> 01:54:12,660
To not create unrest.

1267
01:54:14,960 --> 01:54:17,750
Even the things he knows,
he speaks in his manners.

1268
01:54:18,160 --> 01:54:20,900
His situation puts him under shame.

1269
01:54:21,280 --> 01:54:22,240
That's how, Malhun.

1270
01:54:24,360 --> 01:54:25,940
You stay close to him.

1271
01:54:27,300 --> 01:54:29,120
Barkın must be sharpening his blade.

1272
01:54:30,520 --> 01:54:31,800
As you order, my bey.

1273
01:54:36,500 --> 01:54:38,920
İbrahim Fakih.

1274
01:54:39,760 --> 01:54:41,540
Who stepped into his shadow?

1275
01:54:42,080 --> 01:54:44,100
Who did he talk to?

1276
01:54:44,500 --> 01:54:47,940
He was talking closely with Barkın Bey.

1277
01:54:51,480 --> 01:54:53,220
They were together all the time.

1278
01:54:53,580 --> 01:54:55,200
Who else was there?

1279
01:54:56,280 --> 01:54:58,120
No one that is important, my bey.

1280
01:54:58,160 --> 01:54:59,580
What did he do after leaving?

1281
01:55:00,860 --> 01:55:02,920
Nothing suspicious on the road, my bey.

1282
01:55:03,240 --> 01:55:04,760
But...

1283
01:55:06,500 --> 01:55:09,080
we lost his trace near İnegöl.

1284
01:55:15,760 --> 01:55:17,500
İbrahim Fakih.

1285
01:55:18,620 --> 01:55:20,480
What are you after?

1286
01:55:21,900 --> 01:55:24,600
Enough to avoid the alps following you...

1287
01:55:30,540 --> 01:55:31,620
Go on.

1288
01:55:32,260 --> 01:55:33,340
You can leave.

1289
01:55:45,300 --> 01:55:48,540
Nothing happens out of our will.

1290
01:55:49,960 --> 01:55:53,880
In the west; lands, castles, even
cities...

1291
01:55:53,900 --> 01:55:56,140
change hands through marriages.

1292
01:55:56,940 --> 01:55:59,240
You will be the ruler of
the two tribes...

1293
01:55:59,240 --> 01:56:03,060
through a marriage,
just like a westerner.

1294
01:56:03,060 --> 01:56:09,440
Both İhvaz and Umur Bey wanted
a bey like me to rule their tribes.

1295
01:56:13,740 --> 01:56:15,260
May I enter, Barkın Bey?

1296
01:56:16,260 --> 01:56:17,480
Come, Hüsamettin.

1297
01:56:28,480 --> 01:56:29,800
Bad news, sir.

1298
01:56:32,380 --> 01:56:33,660
Say it!

1299
01:56:35,900 --> 01:56:36,860
Turgut Bey.

1300
01:56:37,440 --> 01:56:38,860
He took İnhisar.

1301
01:56:41,880 --> 01:56:44,360
He put his own flag there.

1302
01:56:49,420 --> 01:56:51,180
Turgut is mad.

1303
01:56:51,480 --> 01:56:52,900
He is rivaling Osman.

1304
01:56:53,380 --> 01:56:54,980
Turgut.

1305
01:56:54,980 --> 01:56:59,340
I won't let him ruin my plans
with his fury.

1306
01:57:00,420 --> 01:57:02,320
Even if he is Osman's enemy...

1307
01:57:02,420 --> 01:57:06,220
he'll choke in my darkness if he
messes with my plans.

1308
01:57:10,020 --> 01:57:13,660
Where does Barkın and İbrahim Fakih
know each other from?

1309
01:57:14,060 --> 01:57:17,400
He had Fakih perform the
marriage ceremony.

1310
01:57:19,500 --> 01:57:24,740
When I wasn't in the tribe, he gathered
a council to be a bey.

1311
01:57:29,300 --> 01:57:31,520
Who does your sickness help, Malhun?

1312
01:57:35,740 --> 01:57:39,940
To Barkın who wants to win without
anyone objecting to him.

1313
01:57:43,000 --> 01:57:44,810
Do you think it was him, my bey?

1314
01:57:45,680 --> 01:57:47,240
Is that so...

1315
01:57:49,780 --> 01:57:51,140
What about Selvi?

1316
01:57:51,780 --> 01:57:52,980
Selvi too?

1317
01:57:52,980 --> 01:57:54,980
We'll find out.

1318
01:57:56,080 --> 01:57:57,800
We'll find it all out.

1319
01:58:13,620 --> 01:58:16,020
Allah bless your hands, my wife.

1320
01:58:16,220 --> 01:58:17,720
It's delicious.

1321
01:58:17,838 --> 01:58:20,100
It feels like honey.

1322
01:58:20,570 --> 01:58:21,690
Here.

1323
01:58:25,750 --> 01:58:28,500
Enjoy it, Cerkutay.

1324
01:58:29,820 --> 01:58:32,570
Enjoy it, my husband.

1325
01:58:35,650 --> 01:58:39,020
Mashallah to my wife.

1326
01:58:39,170 --> 01:58:42,250
How she listens to her husband!

1327
01:59:02,820 --> 01:59:04,920
This is empty too, Cerkutay.

1328
01:59:08,370 --> 01:59:10,470
Do you want me to bring
another pot?

1329
01:59:10,670 --> 01:59:14,320
That soup won't satisfy me at all.

1330
01:59:16,320 --> 01:59:21,200
Cook meaty bulghur so that
we can satisfy our hunger.

1331
01:59:48,300 --> 01:59:50,520
Did you cook it before?

1332
01:59:52,000 --> 01:59:54,770
Mad girl knows her husband.

1333
02:00:12,800 --> 02:00:13,950
It's empty.

1334
02:00:13,950 --> 02:00:16,070
Yes, it is.

1335
02:00:17,320 --> 02:00:20,620
You have eaten everything in the tent,
Cerkutay!

1336
02:00:21,520 --> 02:00:25,670
If you are still hungry, go cook yourself!

1337
02:00:26,320 --> 02:00:27,920
I have things to do!

1338
02:00:31,800 --> 02:00:33,500
Clear the table as well!

1339
02:00:37,220 --> 02:00:39,580
How can you be so relentless
to your husband?

1340
02:00:40,150 --> 02:00:42,670
Can't you give me some food?

1341
02:00:52,020 --> 02:00:53,850
I told Mother Selcan that...

1342
02:00:54,220 --> 02:00:57,370
...a cup of honey wasn't enough!
We needed honey full of hive!

1343
02:00:57,770 --> 02:00:59,870
Now I suffer.

1344
02:01:00,900 --> 02:01:03,120
Oh, mad girl!

1345
02:01:19,700 --> 02:01:21,070
Harmankaya Castle.

1346
02:01:22,700 --> 02:01:26,500
I couldn't attend your feast, but...

1347
02:01:27,970 --> 02:01:31,820
Turgut Bey, I want to make an
agreement with you.

1348
02:01:32,470 --> 02:01:33,820
Have a seat please.

1349
02:01:38,520 --> 02:01:39,920
I should state that...

1350
02:01:40,950 --> 02:01:44,050
If you have your hand in the
death of Mari...

1351
02:01:45,620 --> 02:01:46,800
Talk Nicola...

1352
02:01:47,720 --> 02:01:49,900
So that I kill you.

1353
02:01:53,550 --> 02:01:57,070
Turgut Bey, why would I want to kill her?

1354
02:01:58,100 --> 02:02:03,000
Why would I wait so much to
kill her if I wanted her dead?

1355
02:02:05,270 --> 02:02:07,100
Turgut, please!

1356
02:02:11,550 --> 02:02:13,470
Will you calm down please?

1357
02:02:17,200 --> 02:02:21,220
If he played a role in Mari's death...

1358
02:02:24,320 --> 02:02:26,500
I wouldn't let him live.

1359
02:02:32,900 --> 02:02:33,820
Please.

1360
02:02:40,170 --> 02:02:42,370
Keep her name out of your mouth.

1361
02:02:42,770 --> 02:02:44,370
Never ever again.

1362
02:02:54,100 --> 02:02:56,200
Okay Turgut Bey.

1363
02:02:58,720 --> 02:03:02,850
Just listen what the agreement is about,
at least.

1364
02:03:06,720 --> 02:03:11,350
I offer to use Inegol and Harmankaya
bazaars collectively.

1365
02:03:14,420 --> 02:03:19,950
Both your lives and your goods will be
safe in Inegol Bazaar.

1366
02:03:19,950 --> 02:03:21,070
I assure you.

1367
02:03:21,370 --> 02:03:24,570
I want to make a written agreement...

1368
02:03:26,970 --> 02:03:29,450
...so you have no doubt in your mind.

1369
02:03:29,450 --> 02:03:30,800
Here.

1370
02:03:46,500 --> 02:03:50,300
Common usage of the bazaars will benefit
both sides.

1371
02:03:50,720 --> 02:03:54,170
Once we provide the security...

1372
02:03:54,550 --> 02:03:57,720
...all the merchants around the world
will rush into our bazaar.

1373
02:04:11,700 --> 02:04:17,350
If you accept my conditions, all of those
will happen, Kossess.

1374
02:04:18,920 --> 02:04:21,220
If you abide by my conditions.

1375
02:04:22,950 --> 02:04:25,970
Inegol Bazaar is a great opportunity
for you, Turgut Bey.

1376
02:04:26,350 --> 02:04:29,920
Especially at these times when
Turks are poor.

1377
02:04:30,120 --> 02:04:35,670
At this way, Turkmens will not have to
rely on Osman who only thinks of himself.

1378
02:04:36,050 --> 02:04:37,320
Right?

1379
02:04:49,900 --> 02:04:54,170
A Bey should seek for opportunities.

1380
02:04:58,820 --> 02:05:00,350
Right, Barkın?

1381
02:05:04,050 --> 02:05:05,420
So, my Bey...

1382
02:05:06,500 --> 02:05:08,150
They acted when I was sick...

1383
02:05:08,400 --> 02:05:12,620
...and you were away.
Like there was no other time.

1384
02:05:19,450 --> 02:05:21,800
I act when you are absent, sister.

1385
02:05:22,450 --> 02:05:25,470
Should I have gotten you up from
your sick bed?

1386
02:05:29,820 --> 02:05:31,600
Selvi Hatun is right.

1387
02:05:31,800 --> 02:05:37,820
But if Barkın Bey invited only the Beys
who would vote for him...

1388
02:05:38,500 --> 02:05:40,500
...I can change my mind then.

1389
02:05:48,000 --> 02:05:49,620
I didn't invite anyone.

1390
02:05:52,800 --> 02:05:55,370
I just attended.

1391
02:05:56,600 --> 02:05:59,010
They thought I was suitable
for the Bey position.

1392
02:05:59,570 --> 02:06:01,470
And I didn't refuse it.

1393
02:06:02,550 --> 02:06:06,520
He gave away gold to Beys beforehand.
He deceived them.

1394
02:06:10,900 --> 02:06:13,120
Is this right, Ibrahim Fakih?

1395
02:06:13,470 --> 02:06:15,500
It was Umur Bey's gold.

1396
02:06:18,800 --> 02:06:20,170
It's his bequest.

1397
02:06:20,670 --> 02:06:23,500
He told me to share it to
his family and Beys.

1398
02:06:24,220 --> 02:06:26,200
There's your share too.

1399
02:06:27,220 --> 02:06:29,020
There's no question that
I can't answer.

1400
02:06:29,320 --> 02:06:31,270
But if you are to ask questions...

1401
02:06:32,020 --> 02:06:36,070
you have to ask it to Turgut.

1402
02:06:43,070 --> 02:06:44,770
You are right, Barkin.

1403
02:06:47,470 --> 02:06:49,320
You do things without us.

1404
02:06:51,650 --> 02:06:53,800
But you stand behind us.

1405
02:06:59,750 --> 02:07:01,320
That Turgut Bey...

1406
02:07:02,420 --> 02:07:04,000
He went too far.

1407
02:07:05,200 --> 02:07:08,700
Now he will claim the castle
and gain strength.

1408
02:07:09,620 --> 02:07:11,900
He'll face us some day.

1409
02:07:14,670 --> 02:07:17,520
I'll cut him down before
he grows too much.

1410
02:07:21,170 --> 02:07:23,900
Regulation requires this, Osman Bey.

1411
02:07:24,520 --> 02:07:26,950
Having two leaders is not appropriate.

1412
02:07:33,120 --> 02:07:35,170
You are right.

1413
02:07:37,170 --> 02:07:39,670
You are right Ibrahim Fakih.

1414
02:07:42,900 --> 02:07:47,770
You heal us with your hand
and your words.

1415
02:07:53,070 --> 02:07:57,170
May Allah bless you, Ibrahim Fakih.
You healed my sheikh.

1416
02:07:57,670 --> 02:08:02,220
I am just an occasion.
Heal comes from Allah.

1417
02:08:24,020 --> 02:08:28,550
So, what do you want in return, Nikola?

1418
02:08:30,950 --> 02:08:35,200
You'll give Inhisar to me.

1419
02:08:41,170 --> 02:08:43,250
I will pay you tax.

1420
02:08:48,820 --> 02:08:50,020
Turgut Bey.

1421
02:08:50,270 --> 02:08:55,670
A Turk cannot be imprisoned in
a stone castle.

1422
02:09:04,200 --> 02:09:07,200
Only Turgut can make this decision.

1423
02:10:33,920 --> 02:10:38,320
That Turgut Bey...
From whom he gains his glory?

1424
02:10:40,700 --> 02:10:44,620
He faces all those Lords and Emperor
with his tiny tribe.

1425
02:10:45,070 --> 02:10:47,300
He must have an ally.

1426
02:10:50,500 --> 02:10:52,650
Kossess killed my brother.

1427
02:10:53,270 --> 02:10:56,400
And Nikola is chasing a chance to
backstab us.

1428
02:10:57,470 --> 02:10:59,500
Maybe they are working together.

1429
02:11:02,400 --> 02:11:04,600
The others are our nemesis'

1430
02:11:05,570 --> 02:11:07,520
We were together for politics.

1431
02:11:10,870 --> 02:11:12,800
But that Turgut...

1432
02:11:15,150 --> 02:11:17,100
He backstabbed me.

1433
02:11:18,670 --> 02:11:20,500
He joined the enemy...

1434
02:11:21,070 --> 02:11:25,250
...he conquered Inhisar castle, where
I have been yearning for.

1435
02:11:28,300 --> 02:11:30,050
What is your plan Osman Bey?

1436
02:11:30,470 --> 02:11:33,470
I am always with you, as the leader
of two huge tribes.

1437
02:11:36,670 --> 02:11:38,500
Eyvallah Barkin.

1438
02:11:41,070 --> 02:11:43,120
My move is obvious.

1439
02:11:46,550 --> 02:11:51,120
I will take Inhisar castle back
from Turgut Bey.

1440
02:11:55,320 --> 02:11:57,100
I'll claim his tribe.

1441
02:11:58,020 --> 02:12:02,500
I will exile him from these lands
with no horse or sandals!

1442
02:12:08,650 --> 02:12:11,400
Traitors must pay.

1443
02:12:17,500 --> 02:12:18,850
However...

1444
02:12:20,850 --> 02:12:22,000
Before this...

1445
02:12:24,350 --> 02:12:27,900
I will brighten the suspicious death
of Umur Bey.

1446
02:12:35,120 --> 02:12:37,550
Whoever did this...

1447
02:12:39,200 --> 02:12:42,850
I will shed their blood in sterams!

1448
02:12:45,800 --> 02:12:49,300
They have been cruel.

1449
02:12:52,470 --> 02:12:54,720
They are going to be perished.

1450
02:12:56,970 --> 02:12:58,650
They have already been, my Bey.

1451
02:12:59,200 --> 02:13:00,820
I killed Mongols with my hands.

1452
02:13:01,570 --> 02:13:03,600
I am not talking about that, Barkın.

1453
02:13:11,400 --> 02:13:12,950
I am not talking about that.

1454
02:13:25,620 --> 02:13:27,800
Osman!

1455
02:13:29,300 --> 02:13:32,400
- Osman!
- Mother?

1456
02:13:33,170 --> 02:13:36,200
Osman! Osman!

1457
02:13:36,900 --> 02:13:37,800
Osman!

1458
02:13:38,620 --> 02:13:40,250
- Mother!
- Mother!

1459
02:13:40,550 --> 02:13:42,570
Mother!

1460
02:13:43,800 --> 02:13:44,770
Mother!

1461
02:13:45,800 --> 02:13:48,370
Mother!
Who did tihs?

1462
02:13:49,550 --> 02:13:50,970
Who did this?

1463
02:14:07,800 --> 02:14:09,200
Who did this?

1464
02:14:12,370 --> 02:14:13,470
Who?

1465
02:14:16,470 --> 02:14:18,320
Who?

1466
02:14:26,532 --> 02:14:42,012
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com